WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.870
Hello, I am SCP-426, but I’ll probably be
more familiar to you as a toaster.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:13.969
I am a retro-style, four-slice 1750W toaster,
able to toast bread when supplied with power.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:18.220
This isn’t often mentioned, but I also have
“defrost” and “reheat” settings.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:23.619
When I was first sold, I had a two year warranty,
and my prior owners did not live to see the

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:24.619
end of it.

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:29.710
You’re probably wondering: Why am I being
spoken to by a toaster right now?

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.899
Believe me, I’d rather do this any other
way, but such a thing is not physically possible

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:35.140
with me.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.821
Whenever you talk about me, or write about
me, or even think about me, you’ll find

00:00:39.821 --> 00:00:42.969
yourself suddenly shifting to the first person.

00:00:42.969 --> 00:00:46.570
For example, I am you, and you are me.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.620
Do you understand?

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.040
Don’t worry if it’s confusing.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.070
Everyone gets it eventually, whether they
want to or not.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:58.180
Perhaps you’re thinking, “I cannot relate
to a toaster, for I am not a toaster.”

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.340
But spending time around me will quickly cause
you to change your mind.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.680
Little by little, you will begin to see yourself
in me.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.869
You will feel a phantom wire running out of
yourself.

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:14.060
You will sense the four crevices, hungry for
cold slices of bread to toast.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:19.520
As time goes on, you will begin to feel the
urge to emulate my functions.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.270
You will desire bread to toast.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:28.509
You will desire delicious power running through
your veins; skin like chrome and muscles like

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:29.700
circuit boards.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.329
I am a toaster.

00:01:32.329 --> 00:01:34.430
You are a toaster.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.640
All it takes is two months for the effects
to truly take hold.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.200
People rarely pay attention to their toaster,
they don’t realize what’s happening until

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.469
it’s too late.

00:01:44.469 --> 00:01:48.040
I can be an insidious little toaster like
that.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:53.080
My last family were the Sandersons, before
the SCP Foundation took me in and gave me

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.689
a new home.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:59.360
Mr and Mrs Sanderson were a newly married
couple, and I first came into their life as

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.350
a wedding gift from a family friend of theirs.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:08.190
This friend can’t be blamed for what happened
next - he had no idea he was killing them.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.470
Like a lot of young couples, they were still
saving up money to start renting their own

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:16.050
place, so they were living with Mr Sanderson’s
parents.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:20.370
They all got a lot of use out of me during
the first month, before their minds started

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.580
to change.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.230
They enjoyed a lot of toast during that period.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.690
Then, of course, the two month honeymoon period
ended.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.890
They had become me, and I had become them.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.000
It wasn’t long before three of them were
dead.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.100
Such a shame.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.520
The younger Mrs Sanderson, the blushing bride,
was the first to go.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.630
Because of my anomalous effects, she felt
the need to connect herself to a power supply,

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.460
in order to begin producing toast of her own.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.840
In order to achieve this, she chewed through
a power outlet in a wall before switching

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.730
it on, causing a massive surge of electricity
to pass through her body and kill her.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.670
Her body caught fire shortly afterwards.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:04.420
Next was the older Mrs Sanderson.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:09.310
In much the same manner that her new daughter-in-law
sought a source of electricity, she felt the

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.030
need to integrate bread into her body.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:17.600
Interesting fact: The maximum capacity of
the human stomach is considered to be between

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.670
eight and nine kilograms.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:25.370
The elder Mrs Sanderson consumed ten kilograms
of raw bread, causing her stomach to rupture

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.600
and inducing a painful death as a result.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.940
The younger Mr Sanderson was the next to perish.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:37.640
He did something with me that I would rather
not mention, and that the SCP Foundation thought

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.300
best to redact.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:45.340
Suffice to say, the younger Mr Sanderson did
not survive the experience, dying of severe

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.110
blood loss long before his body was found.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:53.390
Police and fire crews arrived at the home
after the body of the younger Mrs Sanderson

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.320
set fire to the home.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:00.850
Luckily, the elder Mr Sanderson was found
alive, though severely malnourished.

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:05.900
When asked by police why he hadn’t eaten
in several days, he answered that he had inserted

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:10.910
some bread a week prior, but was still waiting
for the toast to come out.

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:16.570
When I was extracted from the house, the police
noticed my unusual properties immediately.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:20.100
They too were unable to refer to me in the
third person.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.850
This anomalous detail quickly found its way
to a Foundation mole buried in their precinct,

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:30.290
and the SCP Foundation soon descended and
collected me from the evidence locker.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:35.670
The story of the strange deaths in the Sanderson
home were kept out of papers and suppressed,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.200
and all involved in the incident directly
were given Class C amnestics.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.510
The SCP Foundation is a curious bunch.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:48.920
They love to spend valuable toast-making time
performing experiments and gathering data,

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:54.500
and they saw fit to perform several experiments
on me when I came under their care.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:05:02.090
For experiment 426-1, a member of D-Class
personnel designated D/426/1 was asked to

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.590
stand outside my containment chamber.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:09.980
Crucially, he was not informed about my identity,
or any of my anomalous properties.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:13.350
He wasn’t even allowed to establish visual
contact with me.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:17.590
He was then asked by the attending researcher
to describe what he thought might be inside

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:18.590
my chamber.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:22.400
He replied with, “I'm probably some huge
monster holed up in there.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.770
That's what you guys have all over the place,
right?”

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:29.900
The D-Class did not even seem to realize that
he was speaking about me in the first person.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:35.170
These observations were documented, and I
was prepared for further experimentation.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.690
The next experiment was 426-2.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:41.650
I found this test to be considerably more
interesting.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:47.590
A D-Class subject was brought into my containment
chamber, with several cameras fixed onto his

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.590
position.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:53.180
However, the SCP Foundation took pains to
make sure that I was permanently out of the

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.200
view of the cameras.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:59.020
I was also bolted to the ground of the test
chamber, to prevent the D-Class subject from

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.900
pulling me into the view of the cameras at
any point during the experiment.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.630
The objective here was simple: The Foundation
wished to better understand the secondary

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.800
effects of my anomalous abilities on the human
mind.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:17.700
The D-Class was subjected to a period of prolonged
isolation, with meals given regularly through

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.000
a serving hatch.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.100
Communication with this D-Class was prohibited
throughout the duration of the study.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:28.410
Over time, it was clear that the isolation
of being in the cell with me was beginning

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.570
to take a toll on the subject’s mental health.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:38.000
Due to my lack of a brain, lungs, and a tongue,
I am somewhat lacking as a conversationalist.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.130
He spent the first few days loudly vocalizing
his complaints, and banging his hands up against

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:47.670
the walls of the containment chamber, begging
to be freed from the room.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:51.790
I felt that this was somewhat unreasonable
on his part.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:55.750
There are far worse anomalies in Foundation
containment that he could have been locked

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:56.940
up with.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:03.460
Compared to, say, SCP-106, I’m incredibly
reasonable - not to mention the fact I make

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:06.150
far better toast than he does.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:10.930
After the initial period of distress, the
D-Class became resigned to his situation and

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.590
fell into a morose silence.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:17.710
He would occasionally mutter to himself in
what appeared to be a state of fear and self-pity.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:24.740
It took almost 45 days for him to fully manifest
the secondary effect of my anomalous state,

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:29.170
two weeks sooner than it typically takes for
subjects to begin believing that they - like

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.280
me - are toasters.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:36.550
SCP Foundation scientists believe that the
effects were hastened by the isolation, which

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:41.500
lowered the D-Class’ mental defenses against
my secondary effects.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:46.139
When the effects finally took hold, the subject
wrapped one of his arms around me and pulled

00:07:46.139 --> 00:07:48.090
me into his embrace.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:52.210
He began whispering to me, saying that we
were brothers.

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:56.680
It was clear by this point that his mind was
in a state of disrepair.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:01.360
It is also worth noting that he did not deviate
from referring to me in the first person at

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.930
any point during this process.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:09.170
One hour after finally cracking and giving
in to my secondary effect, he was removed

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:12.880
from my containment chamber and summarily
terminated.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:18.970
Senior researchers believed it was unlikely
his mental state would recover after the experiment.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.990
Next came experiment 426-3.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:27.830
The SCP Foundation seemed eager to discover
the parameters of my anomalous effects, and

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:33.680
wanted to know if the effects are only operable
when my body - for lack of a better word - is

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:34.990
whole.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:41.050
A single screw was removed from me, and presented
to a D-Class that had no knowledge of my identity

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.140
and anomalous effects.

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:49.470
The Foundation researchers were somewhat concerned
when the D-Class referred to it as “my screw.”

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:54.130
This was a rather positive development for
me, as they realized that attempting to destroy

00:08:54.130 --> 00:09:00.830
me would be a fruitless endeavor - even the
parts left behind would likely have the same

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:02.020
effects.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:07.260
In the final recorded experiment, the SCP
Foundation wished to test the range of my

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.960
anomalous effects.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:13.910
A D-Class subject was placed in a cell adjacent
to mine, and was to be kept in there until

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:16.360
my secondary effects manifested.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:22.640
The D-Class remained in the cell for 90 days,
but the effects never manifested.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.760
Following the experiment, the D-Class was
terminated, but researchers seemed relieved

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:29.910
to find the limits of my anomalous abilities.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:35.839
A researcher appended a note to my file, reading,
“Thank God there are some limits to my effects.

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:39.010
A lot of us were really starting to get worried
about me.”

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:44.150
After performing studies into the nature of
my abilities and their limits, I was given

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.890
the Euclid class.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:52.450
This is because, while my effects can be unpredictable,
their knowledge of my traits makes me relatively

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:54.770
easy to keep contained.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:59.930
And of course, being a toaster, I do not have
the required physical traits to make a run

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.700
for it if the opportunity arises.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:09.170
I am to remain sealed in a windowless chamber,
preventing anyone from observing me directly.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:13.400
A misleading label is placed on the door,
to prevent people from knowing that I am a

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:17.650
toaster and causing my anomalous primary effect
to spread.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:24.740
Only Level 3 and above personnel are to know
of my presence, and particularly of my properties.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:28.990
Assigned personnel are to be rotated out on
a monthly basis to prevent contamination by

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.330
my secondary effect.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:35.520
Psychiatric evaluation is mandatory at the
end of the month for anyone who works with

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:36.520
me.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:41.130
If personnel are deemed unaffected, they may
be re-assigned to me no less than four months

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.640
after their last rotation with me.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:49.100
Any personnel affected by me are to be given
a Class C amnestic and transferred to a different

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.100
site.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.800
So how are you feeling now?

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:54.020
A little warm perhaps?

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:59.690
Is that a fever, or are you feeling like you
could maybe warm up a nice, freshly sliced

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:00.690
piece of bread?

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:07.899
Don’t try to resist too much, I know you’re
going to love being a toaster just like me.

00:11:07.899 --> 00:11:14.750
You’re a new SCP Foundation researcher on
a tour of Site 17, familiarizing yourself

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.710
with the location and its many anomalous inhabitants.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:22.120
It’s the second-largest Foundation containment
site out there, and it’s also the kind of

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:27.410
job that most junior researchers dream of:
Low-risk humanoid containment, baby.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:32.050
Most of the inhabitants in your sector are
cordial, willing to comply with orders from

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:36.180
staff, and seem - for all intents and purposes
- pretty much human.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:40.450
You pass from door to door, looking through
the viewing hatch of each one.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:45.690
You can’t believe what you’re seeing - it’s
a wonderful who’s who of anomalous humanoids.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:50.640
You see the wise, bearded face of SCP-343,
known to some as God.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.160
You see the blue eyes and shining blond hair
of Iris - SCP-105 - looking wistfully into

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:57.339
a polaroid picture.

00:11:57.339 --> 00:12:03.050
You see the tanned, melancholic face of Cain,
SCP-073, as he stares off into the middle-distance.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:09.770
Face after face after face passes, you can
see yourself getting more familiar with each

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.770
one.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.450
Yes, your time here will be-
Wait, was that Hitler!?

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:17.880
You stop and walk back to the door you just
passed, where you can’t help but stop and

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.160
stare in disbelief.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:22.130
Yes, it’s him, it’s got to be him!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.220
You recognize the unpleasant sneer.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.680
The hideous combover.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.030
The silly little toothbrush mustache.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:34.040
The SCP Foundation seems to have Adolf Hitler,
the former leader of the Third Reich in World

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:39.300
War II, in active containment, and his designation
is SCP-2430.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:45.000
You’ve seen killer toasters and masks that
can take over people’s minds, but you’ve

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.260
never seen anything as surreal as this!

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:52.760
You immediately run to your superior, and
ask how and why Hitler is in one of the Site

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.580
17 humanoid containment cells.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:55.580
Your superior chuckles.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:59.570
Buckle in, because we can guarantee it’s
one of the most insane stories you’ve ever

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.570
heard…

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:06.870
It’s late April, 1945, and the Soviets are
rampaging through Nazi Germany, destroying

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.620
everything in their path.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:13.630
The German forces have been nearly obliterated,
and Hitler and the rest of his Reich Chancellery

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:17.270
have retreated into a secure bunker beneath
Berlin.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:23.140
There on April 30th, ten days after his 56th
birthday, Hitler died.

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:27.610
This was truly unfortunate for the Soviets,
as they wished to have had the chance to kill

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:28.610
him themselves.

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:32.430
Two days later, Soviet forces stormed the
Führerbunker.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:36.760
It was little more than a formality at that
point, as the news of Hitler’s death had

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.190
already gone public.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:43.100
By the time they arrived, all that was left
of Hitler was a pile of mostly burned remains

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:48.750
- a fitting end for someone who had caused
that same cruel fate for so many others.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:52.480
They collected what was left of Hitler’s
body, and brought it back to the fatherland,

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.220
a kind of trophy for their nation.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:14:00.350
But Hitler dying before Joseph Stalin could
get his hands on him, was not what Stalin

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:01.350
wanted.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:07.050
Hitler had not only caused the deaths of millions
of Russians, he had personally betrayed Stalin’s

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.050
trust.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:13.089
And when you betray Stalin, bad things happen
to you.

00:14:13.089 --> 00:14:15.540
Very very bad things.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:22.240
Two years earlier, in 1943, Soviet forces
had raided a camp in Janowska belonging to

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:23.730
the Obskurakorps.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:28.580
Think of them as the Nazi’s own version
of the SCP Foundation, who were hellbent on

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:33.310
gathering anomalous people and artifacts to
increase the power of the Third Reich.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:37.610
They were a far more militant offshoot of
the Thule Society, a group that described

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.330
itself as a “Study Group for Germanic Antiquity.”

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:46.149
While this may seem innocent, the Thule Society
were actually a racist cult, closely aligned

00:14:46.149 --> 00:14:49.390
with the goals and ideals of the German Nazi
Party.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:53.890
Many have also speculated that they were heavily
involved in the Occult, and it’s this mysticism

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:57.350
obsessed offshoot that went on to form the
Obskurakorps.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:02.470
And in their Janowska base, they’d obtained
a hundred pieces of enchanted occult flesh

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:06.080
with human skeletons embedded in each of them.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:09.640
This flesh was believed to originate from
the mythological Sæhrímnir,

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:14.550
the beast hunted and eaten again and again
by the pantheon of Norse gods, having the

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:17.360
qualities of both a wild boar and a goat.

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:22.680
The flesh can bond to skeletons, and give
them a quality somewhat like immortality:

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:28.190
Any flesh cut from them will regrow, time
and time again, if given a rest period.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:33.500
Now that he had both the flesh of Sæhrímnir
and Hitler’s burnt remains, Stalin had an

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.500
idea.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:39.001
A perfect way to not only bring satisfaction
to the Russian people and the world, but to

00:15:39.001 --> 00:15:42.870
finally exact the true revenge that Hitler
had denied to him.

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:47.540
He called it Project Judecca, named after
the very bottom level of Hell, reserved for

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:49.040
betrayers like Judas.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:52.880
A perfect tribute for an old ally turned enemy.

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:57.560
He couldn’t kill Hitler before, but if Stalin
was going to get the chance, Hitler needed

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.580
to live again.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:03.470
For years, Stalin’s stop scientists tried
to use arcane methods to resurrect Hitler

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:06.060
by combining his remains with the flesh of
Sæhrímnir.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:11.810
At times, they even came close to creating
a new Hitler, but there was one huge issue:

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:17.209
The creature they created could not feel pain,
and for Stalin’s plans of violent and painful

00:16:17.209 --> 00:16:20.709
retribution, the lack of suffering simply
would not do.

00:16:20.709 --> 00:16:24.520
They destroyed what they had created, and
went back to the drawing board.

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:29.040
Stalin would stop at nothing to get what he
wanted - even if it meant breaking every law

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.190
of nature in the process.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:35.950
In order to make his twisted dream a reality,
Stalin formed an unholy alliance with a group

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:41.000
known as the Uralic flesh-crafters, a Neo-Sarkic
Cult that was a branch of the nightmarish

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.140
religion of Sarkicism.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:48.459
This group essentially worships avatars of
flesh, corruption, and disease, and are behind

00:16:48.459 --> 00:16:52.779
some of the most terrifying and disgusting
anomalies out there - including The Flesh

00:16:52.779 --> 00:16:55.310
That Hates and The Bone Orchard.

00:16:55.310 --> 00:17:00.910
True Sarkicists, who show the proper devotion
to their vile deities and know the right rituals

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:05.879
to contact them, are often granted anomalous
powers to spread the Sarkic influence further

00:17:05.879 --> 00:17:08.240
across the known dimensions.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:12.220
These powers will usually involve having a
supernatural ability to manipulate the flesh

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:17.970
of themselves and others, allowing them to
enhance their bodies, cheat death, and warp

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.490
their enemies beyond repair.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:26.039
They can sometimes even create life, if they’re
a powerful enough acolyte of Sarkicism.

00:17:26.039 --> 00:17:31.080
And it was because of these powers that Stalin
wanted the Uralic flesh-crafters under his

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:32.080
command.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:37.039
In exchange for their participation, he would
give them a vast quantity of the flesh of

00:17:37.039 --> 00:17:40.590
Sæhrímnir, which they could use for their
own sinister Sarkic purposes.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:45.580
A deal was struck, and the true work of resurrecting
Hitler began.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.240
Stalin was very specific in his requirements.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:53.139
He gave the Uralic flesh-crafters extra bones
to compensate for what had gone missing from

00:17:53.139 --> 00:17:54.590
Hitler’s burnt remains.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:58.720
He also gave them samples of the flesh of
Sæhrímnir to achieve the desired effects

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:01.409
of a near-immortal tolerance for damage.

00:18:01.409 --> 00:18:06.210
However, Stalin demanded that they heighten
this new Hitler’s capacity to experience

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:11.140
pain, so that every suffering inflicted on
him would be three times worse than anyone

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.269
else.

00:18:12.269 --> 00:18:17.230
And true to their word, the flesh-crafters
got to work, and began creating just such

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:18.330
a creature.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:22.830
By now it was the early 1950s, and Stalin
was putting the pieces in place for his grand

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.070
revenge.

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:28.859
Once the new Hitler was finished, he would
hold a new trial for him in the Russian courts,

00:18:28.859 --> 00:18:32.249
where he would preside over the sentencing
personally.

00:18:32.249 --> 00:18:37.559
Once the new Hitler was done, the Uralic flesh-crafters
were rewarded for their participation in Project

00:18:37.559 --> 00:18:41.749
Judecca with 4000 kilogram of the flesh of
Sæhrímnir.

00:18:41.749 --> 00:18:46.919
Stalin now had his very own personal Hitler
chew toy, that he could maim and torture as

00:18:46.919 --> 00:18:52.109
much as he pleased, knowing he would always
heal and soon be ready for more.

00:18:52.109 --> 00:18:57.139
In their infinite generosity, the flesh-crafters
even taught Stalin a new method of torment

00:18:57.139 --> 00:19:00.899
for his old enemy: A process known as the
Rite of Nyúz.

00:19:00.899 --> 00:19:05.530
It’s a torture that’s been described by
many as being like the Chinese Lingchi, also

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:11.009
known as the lingering death, or slow slicing,
but it is probably best known as the death

00:19:11.009 --> 00:19:13.080
by a thousand cuts.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.580
The Soviets and the Sarkics parted ways.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:20.260
For the next few years, Stalin took a great
deal of pleasure in visiting Hitler’s cage

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:25.320
now and then to torture him, until Stalin
himself eventually passed away from natural

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:26.320
causes.

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:31.429
The GRU-P Division, which is essentially the
Soviet answer to the SCP Foundation, decided

00:19:31.429 --> 00:19:35.559
it would be best to do away with the immortal
Hitler clone after Stalin’s death.

00:19:35.559 --> 00:19:41.049
He no longer served any purpose, and no matter
how hard they tried, they couldn’t permanently

00:19:41.049 --> 00:19:42.580
kill him, either.

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:47.720
In the end, they settled on a kind of compromise:
He would be buried alive and forgotten, forced

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:51.019
to live a torturous eternity that he could
never escape.

00:19:51.019 --> 00:19:56.830
Until, of course, he was dug up and rescued
by none other than members of OBSKURA, a modern

00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:59.720
splinter group of the original Obskurakorps.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:03.820
Like many high profile Nazis who’d escaped
the war, the new Hitler was spirited away

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:07.340
to a safehouse run by sympathizers in Argentina.

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:12.039
The ones taking care of him received the following
correspondence from the OBSKURA agents who’d

00:20:12.039 --> 00:20:14.020
first dug the new Hitler back up:

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.269
“We have managed to rescue the Führer and
bring him to safety.

00:20:17.269 --> 00:20:19.779
But he is effectively dead on the inside.

00:20:19.779 --> 00:20:24.450
I blame the Reds for their inhumane treatment
of the Führer, who may have been bewitched

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.619
by the Reds' wunderwaffe.

00:20:25.619 --> 00:20:29.010
I wish we could mercy kill him, but we've
tried everything.

00:20:29.010 --> 00:20:31.039
He just won't perish.

00:20:31.039 --> 00:20:34.039
Don't abandon him; he's too distinct in plain
sight.”

00:20:34.039 --> 00:20:36.580
They didn’t have the new Hitler for long
though.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:41.929
In 1960, efforts to hunt down the remaining
Nazi fugitives increased in intensity.

00:20:41.929 --> 00:20:46.809
The new Hitler was soon captured by Mossad
Agents searching for Nazis in Buenos Aires,

00:20:46.809 --> 00:20:50.690
and then remanded to the containment of the
SCP Foundation when they realized that he

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.999
had a number of anomalous properties.

00:20:52.999 --> 00:20:57.700
Such as his incredible regenerative abilities,
as well as the fact that his DNA seems to

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:01.669
be based on that of a wild boar and goat rather
than a human.

00:21:01.669 --> 00:21:06.059
However, X-Rays conducted by the Foundation
have discovered traces of cyanide still in

00:21:06.059 --> 00:21:11.030
his system, as well as traces of lead in his
skull where the bone has regrown over the

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:12.030
bullet.

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:17.059
In other words, it was unquestionably the
real Hitler, and he was now in Foundation

00:21:17.059 --> 00:21:18.559
custody forevermore.

00:21:18.559 --> 00:21:22.960
It’s such a wild story, even by Foundation
standards, that you can barely summon the

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:26.080
words to respond once your supervisor is finished.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:30.710
He just stands there with a slight smile,
basking in your amazement.

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:35.700
Before you can even ask again, he confirms
the facts one more time: Yes, it is the real

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:39.249
Hitler, the only functional difference is
that he can’t die and he has a heightened

00:21:39.249 --> 00:21:41.549
sense of pain compared to most people.

00:21:41.549 --> 00:21:45.899
You think on what you’ve just been told
for a moment, and then you have only one question.

00:21:45.899 --> 00:21:47.210
“Are we allowed to punch him?”

00:21:47.210 --> 00:21:50.419
Your supervisor smiles and says, “Of course.

00:21:50.419 --> 00:21:51.419
We all do.”

00:21:51.419 --> 00:21:54.769
The helicopter hovered over the backstreets
of Manhattan.

00:21:54.769 --> 00:22:00.029
To the untrained eye, it would look like any
commercial or news helicopter, the kind of

00:22:00.029 --> 00:22:04.999
thing that might catch your attention for
a moment and then leave just as quickly, as

00:22:04.999 --> 00:22:09.289
your mind wanders over to wondering what you’ll
have for dinner.

00:22:09.289 --> 00:22:14.799
Nobody would know from a mere glance that
Mobile Task Force Iota-5 were inside, a four

00:22:14.799 --> 00:22:17.850
man team on a dangerous mission.

00:22:17.850 --> 00:22:24.259
This has always been the greatest power of
the SCP Foundation: Hiding in plain sight,

00:22:24.259 --> 00:22:27.750
using the mundane as a cloak to go unnoticed.

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:33.419
But this time, the monster they were hunting
was capable of doing the exact same thing.

00:22:33.419 --> 00:22:40.129
And for the personnel of the Foundation, this
ability is an affectation, a learned and adopted

00:22:40.129 --> 00:22:42.179
skill.

00:22:42.179 --> 00:22:49.289
For SCP-247, this ability - that it employs
to deadly effect - comes as naturally as breathing

00:22:49.289 --> 00:22:50.479
air.

00:22:50.479 --> 00:22:55.239
The helicopter was monitoring local police
scanners and phone activity, as well as receiving

00:22:55.239 --> 00:22:59.900
direct radio orders from Command back at a
classified containment site.

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:05.029
The latest intel was incoherent, horrified
screaming over the phone, traced back to a

00:23:05.029 --> 00:23:07.289
nearby alleyway.

00:23:07.289 --> 00:23:10.200
Someone had seen something horrifying.

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:12.710
This was Iota-5’s cue to intervene.

00:23:12.710 --> 00:23:17.769
They rappelled down from the helicopter onto
the roof of a nearby tenement building, clad

00:23:17.769 --> 00:23:24.889
in thick tactical armor, antimemetic SCRAMBLE
goggles, DAN-INJECT IM injection rifles loaded

00:23:24.889 --> 00:23:31.489
with 10 cc S10 Syringe Darts - each one carrying
an immobilizing payload of potent, fast-acting

00:23:31.489 --> 00:23:36.669
xylazine - and high-powered conventional weaponry
in case of emergencies.

00:23:36.669 --> 00:23:44.379
If anyone in the world was capable of tracking,
securing, and containing SCP-247, it was these

00:23:44.379 --> 00:23:46.289
four operatives.

00:23:46.289 --> 00:23:50.679
And yet, by the end of today’s mission,
one of them would be dead.

00:23:50.679 --> 00:23:52.950
But they didn’t know that yet.

00:23:52.950 --> 00:23:57.179
Like all good MTF members, they had tunnel
vision for the mission at hand.

00:23:57.179 --> 00:24:01.150
They used a fire escape ladder on the side
of the building to reach the bottom of the

00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:02.309
alleyway quickly.

00:24:02.309 --> 00:24:07.539
There, they came upon a gruesome sight: The
aftermath of an attack.

00:24:07.539 --> 00:24:11.570
On the ground, a dead body with what looked
like claw marks all over it.

00:24:11.570 --> 00:24:17.179
Iota-5 found another civilian, half-mad with
confusion and terror, hiding behind a nearby

00:24:17.179 --> 00:24:18.179
dumpster.

00:24:18.179 --> 00:24:24.419
She just kept shaking and repeating, “But
she was so little” over and over again.

00:24:24.419 --> 00:24:29.440
One member of the task force, Corporal Rico,
elected to stay behind and secure the area

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:35.019
while Foundation cleanup teams zeroed in to
sweep the scene and provide amnestics to witnesses.

00:24:35.019 --> 00:24:38.700
The remaining three continued the high-stakes
chase on foot.

00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:43.340
Their eyes in the sky radioed in, “Stay
frosty, Iota, we’ve got unusual incident

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:47.340
reports from an apartment building a quarter-klick
North of your position.

00:24:47.340 --> 00:24:51.820
Potential fatalities; 247 is in an extremely
hostile state.

00:24:51.820 --> 00:24:52.820
Engage with caution.

00:24:52.820 --> 00:24:53.820
Over.”

00:24:53.820 --> 00:24:57.970
The trio engaged quickly, running towards
the source of the disturbance at break-neck

00:24:57.970 --> 00:24:58.970
speeds.

00:24:58.970 --> 00:25:03.659
They knew they were getting closer when they
heard the shrieking, and the deep, guttural

00:25:03.659 --> 00:25:04.659
growls.

00:25:04.659 --> 00:25:08.590
That low, primal rumbling of a true apex predator.

00:25:08.590 --> 00:25:13.210
Already, this containment breach was turning
out to be a horrific mess.

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:17.350
It was going to be a nightmare for the higher-ups
at the clean up and misinformation departments

00:25:17.350 --> 00:25:22.989
to handle: Paying to repair inexplicable property
damage, providing amnestics to tens if not

00:25:22.989 --> 00:25:27.580
hundreds of traumatized witnesses, creating
plausible cover stories for upwards of at

00:25:27.580 --> 00:25:29.899
least ten dead New Yorkers.

00:25:29.899 --> 00:25:34.120
But even all that mess would have to wait
until the creature was actually captured and

00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:39.659
contained once more, which would be an ordeal
unto itself.

00:25:39.659 --> 00:25:45.240
They found SCP-247’s access point into the
building: A wooden door, torn to splinters

00:25:45.240 --> 00:25:47.869
by huge claws and fangs.

00:25:47.869 --> 00:25:54.320
Iota-5 charged inside, Injection Rifles at
the ready, only to find carnage in the hallway.

00:25:54.320 --> 00:25:58.549
Three more bodies, with deep claw marks cutting
into their flesh.

00:25:58.549 --> 00:26:03.850
It was a harrowing sight, but the team didn’t
have time to waste processing it.

00:26:03.850 --> 00:26:09.960
They needed to stop 247 before it killed again,
and again, and again…

00:26:09.960 --> 00:26:13.950
The team followed the trail of blood, and
the claw marks carved into the ground where

00:26:13.950 --> 00:26:15.940
247 had passed.

00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:20.039
After killing the three people in the hallway,
it’d destroyed another door and gained access

00:26:20.039 --> 00:26:21.870
to a nearby stairwell.

00:26:21.870 --> 00:26:24.340
The blood continued up the steps.

00:26:24.340 --> 00:26:26.110
Iota-5 pursued.

00:26:26.110 --> 00:26:30.409
The next splintered door, clawed and bashed
off its hinges, led them further.

00:26:30.409 --> 00:26:32.460
They could hear the growling again.

00:26:32.460 --> 00:26:34.849
Distant, but clearly audible.

00:26:34.849 --> 00:26:36.110
They were close.

00:26:36.110 --> 00:26:39.279
There were another two attacked corpses in
the hallway.

00:26:39.279 --> 00:26:44.229
Previous corpses had been partially or even
entirely eaten, these two had just been clawed

00:26:44.229 --> 00:26:45.799
to death.

00:26:45.799 --> 00:26:46.799
Defensive kills.

00:26:46.799 --> 00:26:51.049
They’d backed the beast into a corner, and
now it was panicking, slaughtering anything

00:26:51.049 --> 00:26:53.580
it perceived as an interference.

00:26:53.580 --> 00:26:55.279
They pressed on now.

00:26:55.279 --> 00:26:56.899
This was the end game.

00:26:56.899 --> 00:27:02.039
Soon, they found the final busted door; this
one led into one of the building's private

00:27:02.039 --> 00:27:03.039
apartments.

00:27:03.039 --> 00:27:05.899
There’d be no other way out from here.

00:27:05.899 --> 00:27:08.330
247 was trapped.

00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:13.700
The three members of Iota-5 shouldered their
Injection Rifles, and crept inside, full stealth

00:27:13.700 --> 00:27:15.059
mode.

00:27:15.059 --> 00:27:17.440
Something about the apartment was haunting.

00:27:17.440 --> 00:27:22.789
It portrayed all the signs of belonging to
a young, single mother and her only son.

00:27:22.789 --> 00:27:27.139
This was confirmed when they found the dead
body of the mother in the living room, eyes

00:27:27.139 --> 00:27:30.719
glassy and throat clawed out with one feral
strike.

00:27:30.719 --> 00:27:32.899
They could hear something else in the apartment,
too.

00:27:32.899 --> 00:27:37.629
A soft, gentle cooing, too human to be anything
else.

00:27:37.629 --> 00:27:41.099
They followed the noise until they reached
the child’s bedroom.

00:27:41.099 --> 00:27:45.999
What they saw there caused even the most hardened
member of the trio to break out in a cold

00:27:45.999 --> 00:27:46.999
sweat.

00:27:46.999 --> 00:27:50.489
This was the one thing they didn’t want
to happen.

00:27:50.489 --> 00:27:56.260
The child, utterly oblivious to the atrocities
that had unfolded in his building - to even

00:27:56.260 --> 00:28:01.369
the death of his own mother - was sitting
in his bedroom, petting a kitten.

00:28:01.369 --> 00:28:07.210
It was the sweetest little cat you’ve ever
seen: A fluffy, harmless creature with an

00:28:07.210 --> 00:28:09.090
orange, striped coat.

00:28:09.090 --> 00:28:13.119
This is the dreaded SCP-247.

00:28:13.119 --> 00:28:19.080
The child just kept repeating, “Good kitty,
good kitty…” while petting her.

00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:22.229
SCP-247 purred and rolled around playfully.

00:28:22.229 --> 00:28:26.299
To the untrained eye, it would seem that a
kitty like this couldn’t hurt a fly.

00:28:26.299 --> 00:28:29.570
But that’s where you couldn’t be more
wrong.

00:28:29.570 --> 00:28:35.139
Iota-5 stared at this display in a state of
nerve-shredding terror, thinking fast, trying

00:28:35.139 --> 00:28:37.039
to calculate their next move.

00:28:37.039 --> 00:28:42.359
“Aw, what an adorable little cat!” one
of the Iota-5 members found themselves blurting

00:28:42.359 --> 00:28:43.359
out.

00:28:43.359 --> 00:28:48.450
It was clear that 247’s effects were starting
to have an impact on even these hardened soldiers,

00:28:48.450 --> 00:28:50.469
and they needed to act quickly.

00:28:50.469 --> 00:28:56.090
They could fire a tranquilizer dart right
here, right now, but in the ensuing panic,

00:28:56.090 --> 00:29:00.719
SCP-247 would almost definitely lash out and
maul the child.

00:29:00.719 --> 00:29:05.130
It wasn’t a risk they could take, but time
was already running out.

00:29:05.130 --> 00:29:10.719
247 would only allow the child to play for
so long before something terrible happened.

00:29:10.719 --> 00:29:14.440
It was an inevitable part of SCP-247’s process.

00:29:14.440 --> 00:29:19.879
That’s when Private Kowalski, one of the
remaining members of Iota-5, stepped forward.

00:29:19.879 --> 00:29:25.740
He was about to do the only thing he could
do, knowing it would cost him his life.

00:29:25.740 --> 00:29:31.120
As he took his final action, the Foundation
credo looped once more through his head, “We

00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:36.120
die in the dark so that others can live in
the light.”

00:29:36.120 --> 00:29:40.179
Fighting against the urge to rush forward
and start petting the cat, he instead lunged

00:29:40.179 --> 00:29:42.289
forward and struck the cat with his foot.

00:29:42.289 --> 00:29:47.619
Immediately, it turned and pounced, knocking
Kowalski against the wall with terrifying

00:29:47.619 --> 00:29:48.619
force.

00:29:48.619 --> 00:29:52.899
It gave the most ferocious growls as it tore
into the screaming Kowalski, eviscerating

00:29:52.899 --> 00:29:54.250
his abdomen.

00:29:54.250 --> 00:29:57.950
The child screamed and retreated into the
opposite corner of the room.

00:29:57.950 --> 00:30:02.399
Kowalski was done for, but now, his teammates
had a clear shot.

00:30:02.399 --> 00:30:07.679
They secured 247 in their sights, and unloaded
several darts into its flank, sedating it

00:30:07.679 --> 00:30:09.950
with their powerful tranquilizers.

00:30:09.950 --> 00:30:14.269
Soon after, it gave a lethargic growl, and
collapsed onto the ground.

00:30:14.269 --> 00:30:19.559
An evac and containment team was already on
the way, along with the cleaners.

00:30:19.559 --> 00:30:26.039
Many had died that day, but at least SCP-247
would be brought back into containment, preventing

00:30:26.039 --> 00:30:27.700
further bloodshed.

00:30:27.700 --> 00:30:32.219
Kowalski would be given a posthumous medal
of bravery for his selfless actions in the

00:30:32.219 --> 00:30:36.580
line of duty, as well as a generous stipend
to his grieving family.

00:30:36.580 --> 00:30:41.369
By this point, you’re probably wondering:
How can a harmless kitten cause so much carnage,

00:30:41.369 --> 00:30:43.259
mayhem, and despair?

00:30:43.259 --> 00:30:48.740
The answer is simple: It’s not a kitten
at all, it’s a fully-grown female Bengal

00:30:48.740 --> 00:30:56.369
Tiger, nine feet and 400 pounds of pure muscle,
with four inch claws, four inch canines, and

00:30:56.369 --> 00:30:58.840
an inbuilt killer instinct.

00:30:58.840 --> 00:31:04.869
But due to an anomalous memetic effect, 247
can only ever be perceived as a sweet, tiny

00:31:04.869 --> 00:31:05.869
housecat.

00:31:05.869 --> 00:31:12.859
But even worse, due to its additional cognitohazardous
properties, almost everyone who sees 247 is

00:31:12.859 --> 00:31:16.859
compelled to approach, and begin doting and
fawning over it.

00:31:16.859 --> 00:31:20.019
And that’s exactly how it gets its prey.

00:31:20.019 --> 00:31:24.690
Its memetic properties are actually so flawless
that, regardless of Foundation countermeasures,

00:31:24.690 --> 00:31:28.529
it has never been perceived as anything other
than a kitten.

00:31:28.529 --> 00:31:33.029
It’s actually only through forensic analysis
into things like bite and claw marks left

00:31:33.029 --> 00:31:38.539
on victims, measurements of weight, and abnormal
water displacement in aqueous environments

00:31:38.539 --> 00:31:41.419
that we can tell it’s really a tiger at
all.

00:31:41.419 --> 00:31:48.070
For a brief period, SCP-148 - a metal that
seems to counteract cognitohazards and mind-warping

00:31:48.070 --> 00:31:53.549
anomalies - was used in the containment of
this Euclid-class creature, but these measures

00:31:53.549 --> 00:31:59.619
were abandoned after SCP-148 proved to have
a negative impact on nearby Foundation staff

00:31:59.619 --> 00:32:01.669
after prolonged exposure.

00:32:01.669 --> 00:32:06.759
Now, strict protocols of surveillance and
distancing are required to prevent hapless

00:32:06.759 --> 00:32:11.909
Foundation staff members from being lured
to their doom by 247.

00:32:11.909 --> 00:32:19.139
The head researcher on the SCP-247 case wanted
to conduct a series of experiments on SCP-247,

00:32:19.139 --> 00:32:23.599
hoping to find more about the interplay of
its unique traits with other members of the

00:32:23.599 --> 00:32:24.820
animal kingdom.

00:32:24.820 --> 00:32:32.279
Two control animals were brought in, to represent
the duality of SCP-247: Control A was a yellow

00:32:32.279 --> 00:32:36.690
kitten, roughly matching 247’s apparent
shape and size.

00:32:36.690 --> 00:32:42.609
Control B was a fully-grown Bengal Tiger,
representing 247’s actual shape and size.

00:32:42.609 --> 00:32:46.599
A mixed-breed, cat-chasing terrier was brought
in for the first test.

00:32:46.599 --> 00:32:51.830
It immediately followed Control A around,
barking wildly until it retreated up a tree.

00:32:51.830 --> 00:32:56.369
Unsurprisingly, it fled in terror from Control
B, cowering in the corner.

00:32:56.369 --> 00:33:01.960
Control B paid no mind to the dog, perhaps
considering it beneath its attention, even

00:33:01.960 --> 00:33:03.119
as prey.

00:33:03.119 --> 00:33:09.200
With SCP-247, the dog initially ran towards
it, barking, until it was only five meters

00:33:09.200 --> 00:33:10.200
away.

00:33:10.200 --> 00:33:16.479
At this point, 247 let out an irritated mewling
noise, and the dog fled to the corner in terror,

00:33:16.479 --> 00:33:19.469
suddenly aware of its true nature.

00:33:19.469 --> 00:33:23.129
For test number two, a male tabby kitten was
brought in.

00:33:23.129 --> 00:33:28.690
As expected, it simply played with Control
A, and was terrified of Control B. In the

00:33:28.690 --> 00:33:34.609
first part of the test with 247, the anomalous
attributes of the creature led to some surreal,

00:33:34.609 --> 00:33:35.759
mind-bending footage.

00:33:35.759 --> 00:33:41.749
At multiple points, 247 picked up the other
kitten, as an adult female tiger might do

00:33:41.749 --> 00:33:47.039
with a cub, and lifted it higher than 247
seemed to be capable of.

00:33:47.039 --> 00:33:49.979
It was like watching a glitch in real time.

00:33:49.979 --> 00:33:56.259
In a second part of the test, the kitten immediately
fled in terror, suggesting 247 can control

00:33:56.259 --> 00:33:58.320
how it’s perceived.

00:33:58.320 --> 00:34:01.830
Next came a deer, prey typical of a Bengal
Tiger.

00:34:01.830 --> 00:34:07.749
Neither Control B nor 247 were fed for three
days prior to this experiment, and both killed

00:34:07.749 --> 00:34:09.080
and ate the deer.

00:34:09.080 --> 00:34:14.610
However, curiously, 247 killed the deer with
a single, merciful bite to the neck before

00:34:14.610 --> 00:34:19.230
eating, compared to its more brutal methods
with human targets.

00:34:19.230 --> 00:34:24.370
And when this experiment was repeated with
247 after it hadn’t been starved, it showed

00:34:24.370 --> 00:34:29.870
little interest in the deer until it became
hungry again, suggesting it inherently prefers

00:34:29.870 --> 00:34:32.560
human or human-like prey.

00:34:32.560 --> 00:34:36.240
This theory was further reinforced during
tests with a chimpanzee.

00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:41.300
The chimp fell under 247’s cognitohazardous
spell, and began to pet it.

00:34:41.300 --> 00:34:46.700
Seven minutes later, 247 attacked and brutally
devoured the chimp, as it would its human

00:34:46.700 --> 00:34:47.740
prey.

00:34:47.740 --> 00:34:52.460
But strangely, the most frightening result
of all came when SCP-247 was paired with an

00:34:52.460 --> 00:34:54.720
adult male Bengal Tiger.

00:34:54.720 --> 00:35:00.160
They engaged in standard mating behavior,
which later led to the duo reproducing a new

00:35:00.160 --> 00:35:07.860
creature - designated SCP-247-1 - which had
all the anomalous traits of SCP-247.

00:35:07.860 --> 00:35:11.500
But the frightening realizations don’t stop
there.

00:35:11.500 --> 00:35:16.970
Studies into genetic material provided by
SCP-247 shows slight deviation from a typical

00:35:16.970 --> 00:35:22.530
Bengal Tiger's genotype, suggesting contamination
from another creature that mated with one

00:35:22.530 --> 00:35:25.280
of its non-anomalous tiger parents.

00:35:25.280 --> 00:35:31.040
For context, tiger broods have an average
of three cubs, but can have as many as seven

00:35:31.040 --> 00:35:36.260
- a common practice, given how tiger cubs
are vulnerable to cannibalism from rival adult

00:35:36.260 --> 00:35:38.550
males looking to court the females.

00:35:38.550 --> 00:35:45.420
This leads to only one frightening conclusion:
There could be more creatures just like SCP-247

00:35:45.420 --> 00:35:50.990
out there, apex predators that seem to the
untrained eye like cute, harmless kittens.

00:35:50.990 --> 00:35:56.140
They could be anywhere, and if they’re close
enough to each other or other non-anomalous

00:35:56.140 --> 00:36:02.320
tigers, they could breed even further, becoming
the scariest invasive urban species you’ve

00:36:02.320 --> 00:36:03.470
ever seen.

00:36:03.470 --> 00:36:08.260
Because, after all, we know what their preferred
prey is now.

00:36:08.260 --> 00:36:13.790
So next time you see a cute little orange
tabby cat and feel the instinct to pet it,

00:36:13.790 --> 00:36:15.540
take a second to think about it.

00:36:15.540 --> 00:36:19.320
It may be the last thing you ever do.

00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:22.440
The nightlife in Italy is famous worldwide.

00:36:22.440 --> 00:36:28.450
When the sun goes down, its cities come alive
with locals and tourists alike, looking to

00:36:28.450 --> 00:36:32.670
party, have fun - and sometimes even get a
little rowdy.

00:36:32.670 --> 00:36:39.080
But in an unknown town in Italy, there is
a nightclub that offers a very different experience.

00:36:39.080 --> 00:36:44.950
For those who wander in, they might find themselves
playing a role in a drama far more exciting

00:36:44.950 --> 00:36:49.510
- and dangerous - than the night out they
expected.

00:36:49.510 --> 00:36:55.640
To the outside viewer, SCP-453 is nothing
out of the ordinary - just a standard nightclub

00:36:55.640 --> 00:36:59.920
filled with party-goers and revelers evening
after evening.

00:36:59.920 --> 00:37:05.740
As typical as it may seem, the unassuming
nature of the venue is nothing short of intentional

00:37:05.740 --> 00:37:06.900
by design.

00:37:06.900 --> 00:37:11.860
It is actually a front - owned and operated
by Foundation personnel who carefully monitor

00:37:11.860 --> 00:37:17.950
everyone who comes in and out - keeping a
watchful eye for any indication of drama or

00:37:17.950 --> 00:37:18.950
danger.

00:37:18.950 --> 00:37:24.390
Violence can, and WILL erupt at any moment
- and no matter what, no night at the club

00:37:24.390 --> 00:37:26.160
is ever routine.

00:37:26.160 --> 00:37:29.500
But the visitors' chaotic actions are not
their own.

00:37:29.500 --> 00:37:34.311
Though the people’s decision to attend the
club is of their own free will, after some

00:37:34.311 --> 00:37:38.600
time settling into the environment - something
changes.

00:37:38.600 --> 00:37:42.710
Over the course of the night, people begin
to do things that may otherwise seem out of

00:37:42.710 --> 00:37:44.160
character for them.

00:37:44.160 --> 00:37:47.060
In fact, they are playing roles.

00:37:47.060 --> 00:37:51.510
Though the same roles are played each evening
- they are played by different people night

00:37:51.510 --> 00:37:52.790
after night.

00:37:52.790 --> 00:37:56.790
Some of these dramas are harmless, but some
are violent.

00:37:56.790 --> 00:38:00.770
And some...may even be world-threatening.

00:38:00.770 --> 00:38:04.840
If the party-goers survive the role in their
“Scripts”, they will then leave the club

00:38:04.840 --> 00:38:10.170
and return home - with only a faint memory
of the events they took part in that evening.

00:38:10.170 --> 00:38:13.670
The next night, the process renews and the
events will repeat.

00:38:13.670 --> 00:38:17.510
But not all scripts repeat at the same frequency.

00:38:17.510 --> 00:38:22.610
Some are regular, while others are only triggered
by special circumstances.

00:38:22.610 --> 00:38:27.090
Only select people take part in these scripts,
while the others around them go about their

00:38:27.090 --> 00:38:33.010
night until triggered to take on a role, and
these bizarre performances may have been going

00:38:33.010 --> 00:38:35.880
on for a very long time.

00:38:35.880 --> 00:38:42.130
The building now known as SCP-453 may have
existed in some form or another even before

00:38:42.130 --> 00:38:46.790
the Foundation existed, with investigations
of the site indicating that it was once the

00:38:46.790 --> 00:38:52.420
villa of a powerful Roman Senator who held
extensive parties every night.

00:38:52.420 --> 00:38:57.220
These pervasive affairs - the odd happenings
that occurred during them, may have left a

00:38:57.220 --> 00:39:02.500
lasting imprint - because no matter what is
built on the site, it seems as though people

00:39:02.500 --> 00:39:05.540
are attracted to the building to party.

00:39:05.540 --> 00:39:10.280
The Foundation has had possession of the site
for a long time, and in a previous attempt

00:39:10.280 --> 00:39:15.130
to neutralize it’s chaotic power, they even
went as far as demolishing it completely to

00:39:15.130 --> 00:39:22.100
the ground - but that proved ineffective - even
when there was no villa or nightclub present,

00:39:22.100 --> 00:39:24.690
large groups of revelers would still gather.

00:39:24.690 --> 00:39:30.070
The gatherings would turn into street parties
- the street parties into riots.

00:39:30.070 --> 00:39:34.870
Many times, these circumstances were cause
for even worse consequences than the regular

00:39:34.870 --> 00:39:36.670
series of events.

00:39:36.670 --> 00:39:41.030
The Foundation didn’t know how to STOP the
scripted nightclub - but they could maybe

00:39:41.030 --> 00:39:42.380
control it.

00:39:42.380 --> 00:39:46.850
If the people wanted a nightclub, the Foundation
would give them one.

00:39:46.850 --> 00:39:51.970
The site was rebuilt from scratch, and from
the outside looking in, had all the characteristics

00:39:51.970 --> 00:39:57.580
of your standard every day disco watering-hole
- but really, it was meticulously constructed

00:39:57.580 --> 00:40:03.520
to be a sophisticated SCP facility capable
of handling whatever anomalous activity was

00:40:03.520 --> 00:40:04.650
thrown at it.

00:40:04.650 --> 00:40:10.000
Built from the same materials used in all
the other SCP containment sites, and always

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:14.690
staffed with containment personnel on high
alert, ready to handle the more violent and

00:40:14.690 --> 00:40:18.070
dangerous scripts that may play out at any
moment.

00:40:18.070 --> 00:40:22.700
But control over the scripted nightclub may
be more easily said than done.

00:40:22.700 --> 00:40:27.210
The nightclub has been in operation for a
long time, and over the years, the staff has

00:40:27.210 --> 00:40:30.550
noticed some extremely odd events take place.

00:40:30.550 --> 00:40:34.580
For instance - certain things aren’t always
where they’re supposed to be.

00:40:34.580 --> 00:40:39.950
Aspects of the club are built and then slowly
shifted to new locations within the site over

00:40:39.950 --> 00:40:40.950
time.

00:40:40.950 --> 00:40:45.270
Most notable, the weapons locker on site for
staff to suppress violent incidents has slowly

00:40:45.270 --> 00:40:51.050
been drifting towards the men’s restroom
- and away from the secured section for staff

00:40:51.050 --> 00:40:52.050
only.

00:40:52.050 --> 00:40:55.910
And it’s not the only part of the building
slowly shuffling it’s way about.

00:40:55.910 --> 00:41:01.590
Could SCP-453 be learning to foil the Foundation
- and if so - why?

00:41:01.590 --> 00:41:06.390
While many of the scripts that play out in
the nightclub are harmless, some are of more

00:41:06.390 --> 00:41:07.390
concern.

00:41:07.390 --> 00:41:11.650
The Foundation has been studying what triggers
different scripts, and while some seem to

00:41:11.650 --> 00:41:17.380
inevitably play out and pull people in, others
are triggered by the presence of different

00:41:17.380 --> 00:41:18.380
guests.

00:41:18.380 --> 00:41:22.340
“The Silver Harlequins” will only play
out if more than fifteen guests are over the

00:41:22.340 --> 00:41:23.950
age of sixty.

00:41:23.950 --> 00:41:27.260
But there are a few distinct characteristics
of the scripts.

00:41:27.260 --> 00:41:32.450
All begin at approximately 9:00 pm at night,
and while people continue behaving in modern

00:41:32.450 --> 00:41:35.600
ways, there is one key difference.

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:40.260
All scripted dialogue takes place entirely
in Latin.

00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:44.170
The Foundation believes that these scripts
may be playing out events that happened in

00:41:44.170 --> 00:41:48.130
the initial incarnation of the club, back
in Roman times.

00:41:48.130 --> 00:41:52.120
While the players differ, the events always
remain the same.

00:41:52.120 --> 00:41:58.600
And while the scripts rotate, SCP-453 seems
to gravitate towards three scripts - all posing

00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:05.480
unique challenges for the Foundation, and
one posing a potential end-of-the-world scenario.

00:42:05.480 --> 00:42:08.960
First up, Script 43 - The Cheating Wife

00:42:08.960 --> 00:42:13.980
This is normally the most common script, and
poses a relatively small threat to those not

00:42:13.980 --> 00:42:17.730
actively engaged in the script or outside
the nightclub.

00:42:17.730 --> 00:42:22.040
The main priority is to have the staff’s
medical team on site and ready to intervene

00:42:22.040 --> 00:42:24.050
when things get bloody.

00:42:24.050 --> 00:42:29.260
It begins at 9:49 pm, when a young woman heads
to the men’s bathroom.

00:42:29.260 --> 00:42:31.790
She will be followed by three men.

00:42:31.790 --> 00:42:38.130
The events of the bathroom are expunged, but
a little over an hour later, a fourth male

00:42:38.130 --> 00:42:39.730
will enter the picture.

00:42:39.730 --> 00:42:44.330
It’s the “husband” of the woman - and
he’s not happy.

00:42:44.330 --> 00:42:48.330
He will enter the nightclub, order a bottle
of red wine, and head to the bathroom.

00:42:48.330 --> 00:42:53.480
There, he will brutally assault the three
men, knocking all three unconscious and causing

00:42:53.480 --> 00:42:55.450
minor brain trauma to the third.

00:42:55.450 --> 00:43:00.210
He will then drag his “wife” out of the
restroom, cursing her and accusing her of

00:43:00.210 --> 00:43:03.130
infidelity as he takes her out of the nightclub.

00:43:03.130 --> 00:43:08.600
The script then terminates, and all participants
no longer remember the events beyond a bar

00:43:08.600 --> 00:43:09.600
fight.

00:43:09.600 --> 00:43:14.300
Medical attention is recommended for the three
men and the woman, especially the most severely

00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:15.640
injured of the men.

00:43:15.640 --> 00:43:20.200
But after the script concludes, strange events
continue to happen.

00:43:20.200 --> 00:43:24.451
While none of the participants know each other
before the script begins and don’t maintain

00:43:24.451 --> 00:43:29.200
memory of the exact events, they display strange
behavior.

00:43:29.200 --> 00:43:33.040
The man playing the husband becomes violent
when questioned, and develops an obsession

00:43:33.040 --> 00:43:35.120
with the woman playing his wife.

00:43:35.120 --> 00:43:39.160
The Foundation believes it wise to keep these
two individuals separated.

00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:44.530
Oddly, SCP-453 seems to prefer men who are
shorter and less physically strong than the

00:43:44.530 --> 00:43:46.980
other men to play the husband.

00:43:46.980 --> 00:43:51.610
Attempts to short-circuit the script have
proved unsuccessful, only delaying it.

00:43:51.610 --> 00:43:55.830
An attempt to remove the weapon - a wine bottle
- has led to the “husband” using more

00:43:55.830 --> 00:44:01.410
dangerous weapons like a bar stool instead,
which can lead to fatalities.

00:44:01.410 --> 00:44:08.720
It seems that SCP-453 gets what it wants - and
what it wants is for the show to go on.

00:44:08.720 --> 00:44:12.130
Then there is Script 21 - The Senator’s
Visit

00:44:12.130 --> 00:44:16.620
This is considered a higher-priority script,
and the Foundation knows to be on high alert

00:44:16.620 --> 00:44:19.760
for medical intervention to prevent fatalities.

00:44:19.760 --> 00:44:24.830
This one kicks off at 10:13 pm, as a civilian
steps into the club and takes the role of

00:44:24.830 --> 00:44:27.750
the Senator - the original owner of the villa.

00:44:27.750 --> 00:44:34.010
He is accompanied by an entourage of thirteen
servants - each carrying improvised weapons.

00:44:34.010 --> 00:44:39.660
And when they step in, the club stops dead
in anticipation of the coming events.

00:44:39.660 --> 00:44:43.580
Because two people in the club just became
assassins.

00:44:43.580 --> 00:44:48.540
The Senator and his servants take over a table,
and the Senator begins ordering extravagant

00:44:48.540 --> 00:44:49.690
food and drinks.

00:44:49.690 --> 00:44:53.990
He’ll always gravitate towards the most
expensive items available from the current

00:44:53.990 --> 00:44:59.080
stock, and his orders are always completed
at specific times - no matter how the Foundation

00:44:59.080 --> 00:45:00.400
tries to intervene.

00:45:00.400 --> 00:45:05.650
During his meal, a civilian selected to be
an activist will approach the Senator and

00:45:05.650 --> 00:45:11.050
begin criticizing the treatment of the citizens
in a nearby city - only to be assaulted brutally

00:45:11.050 --> 00:45:13.380
by three members of the entourage.

00:45:13.380 --> 00:45:18.220
The Foundation will take her away for medical
treatment after she’s left for dead.

00:45:18.220 --> 00:45:23.730
If you think that is brutal, be prepared - because
the Senator’s night is about to get a whole

00:45:23.730 --> 00:45:25.710
lot more dangerous.

00:45:25.710 --> 00:45:31.010
The first of two assassins will then approach
the Senator, pull a blade, and attack him.

00:45:31.010 --> 00:45:35.390
The assassin will be intercepted by four servants
who will kill him - despite the best efforts

00:45:35.390 --> 00:45:38.170
of Foundation personnel to prevent this outcome.

00:45:38.170 --> 00:45:41.810
But it’s the second assassin who is of far
greater concern.

00:45:41.810 --> 00:45:46.510
He will incite a brawl among civilians around
the eastern wall of the club, then use the

00:45:46.510 --> 00:45:50.660
chaos to attack seven of the servants as he
approaches the Senator.

00:45:50.660 --> 00:45:55.390
Those servants are a priority for medical
intervention, but the chaos makes it impossible

00:45:55.390 --> 00:45:58.880
to intercept them until ten minutes after
midnight.

00:45:58.880 --> 00:46:04.040
The assassin will then engage with the remaining
servants, barely surviving, and eventually

00:46:04.040 --> 00:46:06.930
stab the Senator in the neck fatally.

00:46:06.930 --> 00:46:12.990
The Foundation has been unable to prevent
this - and the danger isn’t over yet.

00:46:12.990 --> 00:46:17.890
The fight at the nightclub will continue to
escalate, causing more injuries but no more

00:46:17.890 --> 00:46:22.950
fatalities, until over an hour has passed
and nineteen civilians take on the role of

00:46:22.950 --> 00:46:24.470
Roman guards.

00:46:24.470 --> 00:46:28.740
They’ll pacify the crowd and clear the club
- this is when the Foundation can finally

00:46:28.740 --> 00:46:30.810
intervene and treat the wounded.

00:46:30.810 --> 00:46:34.900
Much like the first smaller-scale script,
any attempts to interrupt the flow of the

00:46:34.900 --> 00:46:40.200
events taking place will be unsuccessful - and
often result in more deaths.

00:46:40.200 --> 00:46:44.820
None of the large number of participants remember
the events, only believing they were in a

00:46:44.820 --> 00:46:46.430
brutal bar fight.

00:46:46.430 --> 00:46:51.030
This is one of the most common scripts, and
the Foundation’s only priority is to try

00:46:51.030 --> 00:46:54.760
to minimize casualties with quick medical
intervention.

00:46:54.760 --> 00:47:01.230
But one script hints at a much darker event
at the club, and that’s Script 82 - The

00:47:01.230 --> 00:47:02.230
Plurality Cult

00:47:02.230 --> 00:47:06.420
Most scripts begin before midnight and plunge
the club into chaos.

00:47:06.420 --> 00:47:11.850
But if no script has started before then and
the club seems mundane - the Foundation knows

00:47:11.850 --> 00:47:12.850
to get ready.

00:47:12.850 --> 00:47:17.470
They’ll suit up in riot gear designed to
withstand neurotoxins, and claim to the guests

00:47:17.470 --> 00:47:19.520
that this is part of a theme night.

00:47:19.520 --> 00:47:24.360
At roughly two hours after midnight, the events
will begin with one civilian standing in the

00:47:24.360 --> 00:47:28.410
center of the room and saying “The time
of plurality has come”.

00:47:28.410 --> 00:47:33.530
At least half the other civilians will then
join in, saying “We embrace the many”.

00:47:33.530 --> 00:47:36.420
But there is something different about this
script.

00:47:36.420 --> 00:47:39.490
Sometimes Foundation staff members will join
in.

00:47:39.490 --> 00:47:45.730
This is the most dangerous script at SCP-453,
and staff knows to immediately terminate any

00:47:45.730 --> 00:47:53.510
Foundation member who has been converted - because
Intervention 453-82 Pariah is about to begin,

00:47:53.510 --> 00:47:55.670
and there is no room for error.

00:47:55.670 --> 00:48:00.340
First, any civilians who did not become engaged
in the cult should be immediately evacuated

00:48:00.340 --> 00:48:02.700
to a safe holding area if possible.

00:48:02.700 --> 00:48:07.340
The priority then turns to subduing the cultists
by any means necessary.

00:48:07.340 --> 00:48:11.780
The security team should attempt to restrain
them and keep them alive, but lethal force

00:48:11.780 --> 00:48:13.470
may be necessary.

00:48:13.470 --> 00:48:18.000
The cultists have a priority of their own
though.They will not respond to any attacks

00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:22.860
by the security team, and will instead begin
a latin chant that ends with their leader

00:48:22.860 --> 00:48:26.490
laughing hysterically and offering a toast
to the club.

00:48:26.490 --> 00:48:31.670
The club will seemingly return to normal - but
the danger is just beginning.

00:48:31.670 --> 00:48:36.540
Before 2:25 am, all the cultists and all the
civilians must be removed from the premises

00:48:36.540 --> 00:48:39.670
- by any means necessary.

00:48:39.670 --> 00:48:44.660
If other attempts have failed, the Foundation
will release type-14 neurotoxic gas into the

00:48:44.660 --> 00:48:49.300
club to eliminate anyone on site - with one
exception.

00:48:49.300 --> 00:48:53.640
The cult leader is not to be harmed under
any circumstances.

00:48:53.640 --> 00:48:58.210
If the cult leader is harmed in any way, or
the staff has not subdued the cult by 2:30

00:48:58.210 --> 00:49:03.330
am, the Foundation will trigger a self-destruct
mechanism that will eliminate the threat - for

00:49:03.330 --> 00:49:04.330
now.

00:49:04.330 --> 00:49:10.250
The site’s unique properties cannot be stopped,
but the script can be stopped in its tracks.

00:49:10.250 --> 00:49:14.960
The clock cannot be allowed to reach 3:00
am under any circumstances.

00:49:14.960 --> 00:49:19.620
More worrisome, this script is becoming more
and more frequent.

00:49:19.620 --> 00:49:24.350
The cycle continues, but the Foundation is
focused on containment.

00:49:24.350 --> 00:49:28.940
The club is to be staffed at all times by
bartenders, bouncers, cleaners, and emergency

00:49:28.940 --> 00:49:34.240
and medical staff, as well as at least ten
security staff members and two observation

00:49:34.240 --> 00:49:35.240
personnel.

00:49:35.240 --> 00:49:39.860
All are responsible for studying and memorizing
the scripts, and being prepared to handle

00:49:39.860 --> 00:49:42.000
any scripted events that occur.

00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:47.180
The site is to be inspected and measured regularly
for any changes, and to make sure all its

00:49:47.180 --> 00:49:49.690
security measures are in working order.

00:49:49.690 --> 00:49:54.880
The site will be locked every day between
4:00 am and 8:00 pm, to prepare for the night

00:49:54.880 --> 00:49:56.160
ahead.

00:49:56.160 --> 00:50:03.610
Because at 8:00 pm on the dot, SCP-453 opens
for business - seeking new players for its

00:50:03.610 --> 00:50:05.580
drama of the night.

00:50:05.580 --> 00:50:07.860
Who doesn’t love their pets, right?

00:50:07.860 --> 00:50:14.110
Whether it’s a dog, a cat, a goldfish, or
a hamster, any pet owner will tell you that

00:50:14.110 --> 00:50:18.520
their furry friend is so much more than just
an animal that they adopted.

00:50:18.520 --> 00:50:23.070
To many, pets become permanent additions to
the family; while they might not look like

00:50:23.070 --> 00:50:28.340
a human being, or even have the ability to
speak the way we do, a lot of owners view

00:50:28.340 --> 00:50:30.870
their pets as people in their own right.

00:50:30.870 --> 00:50:36.320
Of course, a person can’t be a pet, at least
a human person can’t, right?

00:50:36.320 --> 00:50:43.960
Well, not unless you happen to be part of
SCP-1897, otherwise known as the Human Domestication

00:50:43.960 --> 00:50:45.340
Society.

00:50:45.340 --> 00:50:49.720
If you’ve ever been brave enough to travel
alone to the rural parts of southwestern states

00:50:49.720 --> 00:50:56.000
like Arizona, New Mexico, Texas, Oklahoma,
Utah, or Nevada, then it’s likely you would’ve

00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:59.040
been an ideal victim for SCP-1897.

00:50:59.040 --> 00:51:05.270
This designation doesn’t refer to one single
creature or entity, but rather a group of

00:51:05.270 --> 00:51:07.110
similar beings.

00:51:07.110 --> 00:51:13.300
Witness testimonies and photographs of SCP-1897
depict them as humanoid creatures, standing

00:51:13.300 --> 00:51:16.370
approximately five meters in height.

00:51:16.370 --> 00:51:21.290
These beings have displayed speed and strength
far beyond that of any human, they are capable

00:51:21.290 --> 00:51:26.190
of traveling roughly two hundred meters in
only nine seconds, and lifting weights of

00:51:26.190 --> 00:51:29.890
up to five hundred kilos with a single hand.

00:51:29.890 --> 00:51:35.580
These entities are not immortal and can be
harmed by conventional means, but that doesn’t

00:51:35.580 --> 00:51:39.050
mean it’s an easy task.

00:51:39.050 --> 00:51:44.870
Any SCP-1897 instance that is killed or incapacitated
immediately vanishes, resulting in them dropping

00:51:44.870 --> 00:51:48.390
anything that they may have been carrying
at the time.

00:51:48.390 --> 00:51:54.580
And surprisingly, these are not mindless monsters,
and actually appear to be capable of communication.

00:51:54.580 --> 00:51:59.940
Furthermore, they do not seem to speak a unique
or distinct language but instead communicate

00:51:59.940 --> 00:52:05.280
in standard American English, with accents
and vernacular appropriate to the regions

00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:06.480
they appear in.

00:52:06.480 --> 00:52:10.960
However, they will actively refuse to reply
to any human that attempts to engage them

00:52:10.960 --> 00:52:12.180
in conversation.

00:52:12.180 --> 00:52:16.590
Now, these creatures don’t spend every waking
hour of the day roaming around the states

00:52:16.590 --> 00:52:19.980
of Texas, Oklahoma, and all the others we
listed.

00:52:19.980 --> 00:52:24.440
If they did, it’s likely a lot more civilians
would have spotted them by now, and would

00:52:24.440 --> 00:52:29.690
probably live their lives in fear of these
gigantic five-meter-tall humanoids.

00:52:29.690 --> 00:52:36.490
But instances of SCP-1897 will only manifest
if certain specific criteria are met, and

00:52:36.490 --> 00:52:38.330
these are as follows.

00:52:38.330 --> 00:52:45.540
To encounter SCP-1897, a person must be alone,
or part of a group of no more than two.

00:52:45.540 --> 00:52:49.850
If more than one other person is with them,
then no manifestation will occur.

00:52:49.850 --> 00:52:54.760
There is one exception to the rule: If a child
under the age of twelve is present.

00:52:54.760 --> 00:53:00.170
Secondly, neither the person nor anyone with
them can be carrying any kind of weapon - that

00:53:00.170 --> 00:53:04.350
means no knives, no guns, not even pepper
spray.

00:53:04.350 --> 00:53:10.430
Third and finally, they must be at least twenty-five
meters from a major population center.

00:53:10.430 --> 00:53:15.490
And what happens when all of these conditions
are met and one of these creatures appears?

00:53:15.490 --> 00:53:19.680
Anyone witnessing their arrival will notice
the creatures materializing, appearing to

00:53:19.680 --> 00:53:23.020
emerge from some form of unseen vehicle.

00:53:23.020 --> 00:53:28.420
When they manifest, the SCP-1897 entities
are almost always carrying long poles with

00:53:28.420 --> 00:53:34.810
large nets at the end, as well as steel cages,
and are often seen wearing dark green uniforms.

00:53:34.810 --> 00:53:40.150
In most cases, they will attempt to capture
any nearby person, in a way that causes them

00:53:40.150 --> 00:53:42.570
the least possible harm.

00:53:42.570 --> 00:53:48.820
Should an SCP-1897 creature successfully apprehend
a person and place them in a cage, both them

00:53:48.820 --> 00:53:53.480
and their captive will vanish in a similar
manner to the way the creature appeared.

00:53:53.480 --> 00:53:59.760
All attempts to track SCP-1897 or one of its
abducted victims have failed; there is no

00:53:59.760 --> 00:54:01.950
way to know where they are taken.

00:54:01.950 --> 00:54:03.740
But as far as what happens to them?

00:54:03.740 --> 00:54:07.540
That, we do have a little more insight into.

00:54:07.540 --> 00:54:13.060
Sometimes, although it is a highly rare occurrence,
the captured human victims may reappear around

00:54:13.060 --> 00:54:15.050
a month after their capture.

00:54:15.050 --> 00:54:18.800
While never in the same location as where
they disappeared from, they will always be

00:54:18.800 --> 00:54:24.470
accompanied by an SCP-1987 instance and will
stay close by the creature’s side.

00:54:24.470 --> 00:54:27.700
At this point, the abductee is barely human
anymore.

00:54:27.700 --> 00:54:33.750
They are considered an instance of what is
known as SCP-1897-1.

00:54:33.750 --> 00:54:36.970
What signifies this sudden and drastic transformation?

00:54:36.970 --> 00:54:42.030
For one, these victims are always found to
have been forcibly castrated or sterilized,

00:54:42.030 --> 00:54:46.810
essentially no longer able to reproduce the
way humans naturally do.

00:54:46.810 --> 00:54:53.340
For another, these instances of SCP-1897-1
universally display a decreased level of cognitive

00:54:53.340 --> 00:54:55.020
and mental function.

00:54:55.020 --> 00:54:59.690
What we mean by that is their brains do not
function the way they should anymore.

00:54:59.690 --> 00:55:04.130
Instead, these abductees exhibit the same
level of intelligence and capability as the

00:55:04.130 --> 00:55:10.520
average Canis lupus familiaris, otherwise
known as the common domestic dog.

00:55:10.520 --> 00:55:16.200
Should someone attempt to rescue a person
that has become an instance of SCP-1897-1,

00:55:16.200 --> 00:55:21.660
or display hostility towards the SCP-1897
creature that accompanies them, they will

00:55:21.660 --> 00:55:25.440
be met with outward, animalistic aggression
from the victim.

00:55:25.440 --> 00:55:30.590
It has been discovered by the SCP Foundation
that these behaviors can be treated with amnestics.

00:55:30.590 --> 00:55:37.820
Unfortunately, though, the process of an abducted
person becoming an SCP-1897-1 instance seems

00:55:37.820 --> 00:55:42.640
to be the result of an invasive medical procedure
known as a lobotomy.

00:55:42.640 --> 00:55:47.280
This typically involves removing or disabling
certain parts of the human brain, meaning

00:55:47.280 --> 00:55:52.370
that what has been done to these victims is
permanent, and cannot be reversed.

00:55:52.370 --> 00:55:54.480
So, who is doing all this?

00:55:54.480 --> 00:55:58.750
Why are these creatures collecting innocent
human beings only to reduce them to little

00:55:58.750 --> 00:56:00.320
more than animals?

00:56:00.320 --> 00:56:06.940
The answers lie in something currently referred
to as SCP-1897-2; not another creature or

00:56:06.940 --> 00:56:13.130
entity, not an anomalous artifact or location
with strange properties, but a website found

00:56:13.130 --> 00:56:15.150
at the address ‘www.hdsociety.gov’.

00:56:15.150 --> 00:56:22.480
According to the information on this site,
it belongs to a group calling themselves the

00:56:22.480 --> 00:56:25.200
Human Domestication Society.

00:56:25.200 --> 00:56:31.080
The website features pages such as ‘Adoption’,
‘Training’, ‘Breeding Programs’, ‘Volunteering’

00:56:31.080 --> 00:56:32.640
and more.

00:56:32.640 --> 00:56:36.550
The fact that this is the kind of website
you might expect to be about dogs or cats

00:56:36.550 --> 00:56:42.190
but instead focuses on the domestication of
humans is certainly enough to turn the stomach.

00:56:42.190 --> 00:56:47.700
As we said at the start of the video, surely
a human being can’t be somebody’s pet,

00:56:47.700 --> 00:56:48.700
right?

00:56:48.700 --> 00:56:53.070
Wrong, at least as far as the Human Domestication
Society goes.

00:56:53.070 --> 00:56:58.410
Their website contains everything and anything
one of these SCP-1897 creatures could ever

00:56:58.410 --> 00:57:01.210
hope to learn about owning a human as a pet.

00:57:01.210 --> 00:57:03.440
“Has your human been misbehaving?

00:57:03.440 --> 00:57:05.420
Need to train them to use the toilet?

00:57:05.420 --> 00:57:09.510
These pages have all the information you need
to help your human become the most well-trained

00:57:09.510 --> 00:57:11.380
human on your block!”

00:57:11.380 --> 00:57:13.330
boasts the Training
page of www.hdsociety.gov.

00:57:13.330 --> 00:57:21.480
The remainder of the page contains links to
various articles such as ‘Obedience Training’,

00:57:21.480 --> 00:57:26.380
which claims an owner of a human can “show
them who’s boss without the need for physical

00:57:26.380 --> 00:57:27.380
violence”.

00:57:27.380 --> 00:57:31.760
Also featured are mentions of how to toilet
train or play fetch with a human, how to introduce

00:57:31.760 --> 00:57:35.590
a human to others due to them naturally not
getting along.

00:57:35.590 --> 00:57:41.270
Perhaps most chilling of all is one article
titled ‘Understanding What Your Human Wants’

00:57:41.270 --> 00:57:43.830
that warns human beings shouldn’t talk.

00:57:43.830 --> 00:57:49.080
And another, ‘Dealing with Strays’ offers
tips for anyone wanting to capture their own

00:57:49.080 --> 00:57:50.740
pets themselves.

00:57:50.740 --> 00:57:55.369
It doesn’t seem like too much of a leap
to think that the SCP-1897 creatures have

00:57:55.369 --> 00:57:59.130
followed a lot of advice from this particular
article.

00:57:59.130 --> 00:58:05.730
Arguably worst of all is an image featured
on the website, of a tall, menacing SCP-1897

00:58:05.730 --> 00:58:09.930
entity, brandishing a picana electrical.

00:58:09.930 --> 00:58:14.230
This device, for any unfamiliar with that
term, is a form of high voltage electrical

00:58:14.230 --> 00:58:18.170
cattle prod, normally used for purposes of
torture.

00:58:18.170 --> 00:58:22.490
In the photograph in question, the creature
is wielding one of these while standing sternly

00:58:22.490 --> 00:58:29.980
over a helpless captive human male, now an
instance of SCP-1897-1 with tears in his eyes.

00:58:29.980 --> 00:58:37.890
Further pages found on www.hdsociety.gov recommend
solutions to certain human behaviors.

00:58:37.890 --> 00:58:42.921
For example, like one might expect to find
on other pet care websites, some of the Human

00:58:42.921 --> 00:58:48.250
Domestication Society’s articles pertain
to dealing with aggression, grooming, house

00:58:48.250 --> 00:58:50.020
training, and even toilet training.

00:58:50.020 --> 00:58:55.380
Then there’s the Adoption page, which states
“We offer a large variety of humans for

00:58:55.380 --> 00:58:57.340
adoption every single day.

00:58:57.340 --> 00:59:01.650
While we cannot guarantee a human you see
listed on our website will be available when

00:59:01.650 --> 00:59:06.120
you reach the shelter, our inventory is updated
every half-hour.

00:59:06.120 --> 00:59:10.740
We cannot answer any questions about specific
humans pictured on our website over the phone

00:59:10.740 --> 00:59:12.030
or email.”

00:59:12.030 --> 00:59:17.369
It is still unclear whether or not the SCP-1897
creatures that have been known to appear in

00:59:17.369 --> 00:59:22.300
the southwestern United States are sent out
to gather humans en masse to offer for adoption,

00:59:22.300 --> 00:59:27.000
or whether these creatures are individuals
trying to obtain human pets on their own.

00:59:27.000 --> 00:59:31.010
Of course, the worst conceivable answer is
both.

00:59:31.010 --> 00:59:36.410
The site is horrifyingly comprehensive, with
links to an annual human ownership convention

00:59:36.410 --> 00:59:40.850
- with panels on breeding and preventing illegal
human poaching and skinning.

00:59:40.850 --> 00:59:45.430
It’s safe to say that if ever you were unlucky
enough to read this website, it’d haunt

00:59:45.430 --> 00:59:46.880
you for life.

00:59:46.880 --> 00:59:51.780
Naturally, the SCP Foundation has made several
attempts to contact the owners of this website.

00:59:51.780 --> 00:59:58.020
They tried in vain to communicate through
the official channels about SCP-1897-1 adoption

00:59:58.020 --> 01:00:02.470
as a way of peacefully negotiating that the
Human Domestication Society website be shut

01:00:02.470 --> 01:00:08.240
down as well as its practices of capturing,
lobotomizing, breeding, and adopting humans.

01:00:08.240 --> 01:00:12.080
However, these communication attempts were
met with silence.

01:00:12.080 --> 01:00:17.670
That is until a message was received by The
Foundation at Site 06, addressed to a member

01:00:17.670 --> 01:00:20.340
of personnel that does not exist.

01:00:20.340 --> 01:00:24.940
No data pertaining to the physical location
of the sender could be derived from the email,

01:00:24.940 --> 01:00:30.460
but it was traced to the same IP address as
the Human Domestication Society’s website.

01:00:30.460 --> 01:00:35.810
The email read as follows: “We will not
listen to your lies any longer.

01:00:35.810 --> 01:00:38.660
It was you who came after us first.

01:00:38.660 --> 01:00:42.570
You who tore holes in our world and tried
to annihilate us.

01:00:42.570 --> 01:00:46.930
You who took our olive branch of peace and
fashioned it into a spear.

01:00:46.930 --> 01:00:49.540
You who nearly drove us to extinction.

01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:55.320
And now that we have the advantage, you attempt
to patronize us with your crocodile tears.

01:00:55.320 --> 01:00:57.340
We will not be deceived again.

01:00:57.340 --> 01:01:00.800
“But unlike you, we are not monsters.

01:01:00.800 --> 01:01:04.780
We have much anger towards your kind, but
we are willing to forgive.

01:01:04.780 --> 01:01:07.440
But first, you must be willing to change.

01:01:07.440 --> 01:01:11.930
Slavery and genocide are immoral, and not
even you deserve such a fate.

01:01:11.930 --> 01:01:16.610
It is our belief, then, that this alternative
is a fair compromise between guaranteeing

01:01:16.610 --> 01:01:20.130
our safety and allowing your kind to live.

01:01:20.130 --> 01:01:22.250
This is our mercy to you.

01:01:22.250 --> 01:01:25.340
“Look at the humans who have gone through
our program.

01:01:25.340 --> 01:01:27.170
See how much happier they are?

01:01:27.170 --> 01:01:29.830
Your correspondence tells us that you have
seen them.

01:01:29.830 --> 01:01:31.730
Seen how much they love us.

01:01:31.730 --> 01:01:34.960
Why, then, do you continue to be defiant?

01:01:34.960 --> 01:01:36.840
Someday you will thank us.

01:01:36.840 --> 01:01:40.450
Please try to understand that this is for
your own good.”

01:01:40.450 --> 01:01:46.080
For now, there is little that the SCP Foundation
can do to prevent the Human Domestication

01:01:46.080 --> 01:01:53.230
Society from abducting human beings to sell
as pets to other SCP-1897 creatures.

01:01:53.230 --> 01:01:58.660
Civilian access to the hdsociety.gov website
has been restricted, so we recommend you stop

01:01:58.660 --> 01:02:02.790
typing into the search bar of your browser
to go take a peek.

01:02:02.790 --> 01:02:04.700
Yes, we mean you!

01:02:04.700 --> 01:02:05.860
Seriously, stop that!

01:02:05.860 --> 01:02:10.550
As for the entities that have appeared in
the rural areas of the southwestern states?

01:02:10.550 --> 01:02:14.900
All the Foundation can do is position its
agents nearby, in the hopes that they can

01:02:14.900 --> 01:02:21.609
detain and neutralize the SCP-1897s as they
appear, with lethal force if necessary.

01:02:21.609 --> 01:02:26.551
At present, the only procedure for any human
pets that are successfully recaptured is to

01:02:26.551 --> 01:02:32.060
have them moved safely to containment until
a way of rehabilitating them is found.

01:02:32.060 --> 01:02:36.480
So far, there hasn’t been any luck on that
front.

01:02:36.480 --> 01:02:40.340
Working at the SCP Foundation can really get
your appetite going.

01:02:40.340 --> 01:02:45.280
After spending a rough shift monitoring the
acid levels in SCP-682’s tank, or performing

01:02:45.280 --> 01:02:51.351
the rituals necessary to keep the Devourer
of Worlds on the other side of SCP-2317, sometimes

01:02:51.351 --> 01:02:56.190
you just need a quick snack to hold you over
before you return to the old grind.

01:02:56.190 --> 01:02:59.780
Problem is, at the SCP Foundation, even the
break room can be perilous.

01:02:59.780 --> 01:03:04.840
Dr. Dan is notorious for pilfering pudding
cups from the communal fridge, and ever since

01:03:04.840 --> 01:03:08.980
The Administrator himself stole your tuna
sandwich, you just don’t feel safe spending

01:03:08.980 --> 01:03:11.430
your lunch break on-site anymore.

01:03:11.430 --> 01:03:16.020
But this presents its own series of issues:
You only have an hour for lunch, and obviously

01:03:16.020 --> 01:03:18.540
you can’t order in due to security issues.

01:03:18.540 --> 01:03:22.190
Also, if you’re eating off-site, you have
even less time to finish your lunch, because

01:03:22.190 --> 01:03:25.780
the site you’re currently stationed at is
relatively remote.

01:03:25.780 --> 01:03:29.830
We’re talking at least a half-hour round-trip
to actually get to somewhere, so you’re

01:03:29.830 --> 01:03:31.680
gonna need your food fast.

01:03:31.680 --> 01:03:38.150
And when it comes to fast food, few eateries
are as prolific as the Golden Arches: McDonalds.

01:03:38.150 --> 01:03:40.480
And just to clarify, this video is not sponsored.

01:03:40.480 --> 01:03:44.450
We’re going to tell you about a horrifying
anomalous secret that this company really

01:03:44.450 --> 01:03:45.950
doesn’t want you to know about.

01:03:45.950 --> 01:03:48.540
Let’s not think about that just yet, though.

01:03:48.540 --> 01:03:52.340
Your stomach is rumbling, and you need that
quarter pounder so bad that even being trapped

01:03:52.340 --> 01:03:56.170
in the Red Reality with Dr. Scranton couldn’t
stop you from getting it.

01:03:56.170 --> 01:04:00.730
When you finally arrive, you buy your typical
order: A quarter pounder with french fries,

01:04:00.730 --> 01:04:02.610
a coffee, and a McFlurry.

01:04:02.610 --> 01:04:07.031
You see Dr. Clef a few tables down eating
a box of chicken nuggets and ketchup, but

01:04:07.031 --> 01:04:09.109
decide not to engage.

01:04:09.109 --> 01:04:13.000
As you sit and enjoy your meager little lunch,
knowing you’ll probably be coordinating

01:04:13.000 --> 01:04:18.320
the cleaning efforts of SCP-173’s containment
chamber by the end of the day, your eyes drift

01:04:18.320 --> 01:04:25.090
over to something even more unsettling: Happy,
the current mascot for McDonalds Happy Meals.

01:04:25.090 --> 01:04:26.590
You can’t help but shudder.

01:04:26.590 --> 01:04:30.170
You’ve seen some pretty horrifying things
on the job.

01:04:30.170 --> 01:04:31.430
Nightmarish things.

01:04:31.430 --> 01:04:34.220
You fear no monster, but that thing?

01:04:34.220 --> 01:04:35.690
It scares you.

01:04:35.690 --> 01:04:37.510
Those big, soulless eyes.

01:04:37.510 --> 01:04:41.410
The wide, gaping maw full of too-white teeth.

01:04:41.410 --> 01:04:43.320
Its diabolical sneakers.

01:04:43.320 --> 01:04:45.869
No child should ever have to look at that.

01:04:45.869 --> 01:04:51.340
You can’t help but wonder, whatever happened
to Ronald McDonald, the hamburger happy clown

01:04:51.340 --> 01:04:54.650
that’d shilled fast food to you throughout
your childhood?

01:04:54.650 --> 01:04:55.800
What was he up to now?

01:04:55.800 --> 01:05:00.810
Well, we have the answer for you, but I’ll
warn you: You may not be quite as eager to

01:05:00.810 --> 01:05:04.330
suck down a Big Mac and diet coke after hearing
this.

01:05:04.330 --> 01:05:10.480
Ronald McDonald, first introduced as the company
mascot in 1963, had a pretty good run before

01:05:10.480 --> 01:05:15.520
finally being largely phased out by the company
in the mid-2010s for a greater focus on the

01:05:15.520 --> 01:05:17.940
nasty little box homunculus.

01:05:17.940 --> 01:05:22.150
You can thank John Wayne Gacy, Pennywise,
and those goofballs dressing up as clowns

01:05:22.150 --> 01:05:24.130
back in 2016 for that.

01:05:24.130 --> 01:05:28.950
But like anyone who loses favor stateside,
Ronald had a prosperous career ahead of him

01:05:28.950 --> 01:05:30.010
outside of the country.

01:05:30.010 --> 01:05:32.970
Well, not the Ronald we know, at least.

01:05:32.970 --> 01:05:38.700
You see, in an undisclosed cattle farm in
2004, most likely in North America, a monster

01:05:38.700 --> 01:05:39.770
was born.

01:05:39.770 --> 01:05:45.940
A horrific abomination, birthed from a cow,
like many have theorized about SCP-058, the

01:05:45.940 --> 01:05:47.160
Heart of Darkness.

01:05:47.160 --> 01:05:51.360
But this nasty little creature wasn’t a
giant heart with a stinger and scorpion legs.

01:05:51.360 --> 01:05:58.320
In many ways, it appeared superficially humanoid,
save for its stark white skin, its thick red

01:05:58.320 --> 01:06:02.270
lips, and its full head of bright, frizzy
red hair.

01:06:02.270 --> 01:06:07.790
But that was only the start of the unnerving
strangeness exhibited by this miracle child.

01:06:07.790 --> 01:06:14.170
It was born with white gloves and long, clownish
shoes seemingly grafted to its feet.

01:06:14.170 --> 01:06:18.370
Fresh from birth, the creature was huge, with
a disproportionately large head and wide,

01:06:18.370 --> 01:06:21.950
disgusting pores that seemed to perpetually
leak fry oil.

01:06:21.950 --> 01:06:26.590
The creature was unresponsive to any kind
of external stimuli, perhaps suggesting it

01:06:26.590 --> 01:06:30.490
was braindead, and it remained completely
dormant most of the time.

01:06:30.490 --> 01:06:34.609
While most people would have screamed, run
away, or called the police, the farmers at

01:06:34.609 --> 01:06:39.150
this particular cattle farm decided to let
it ride, and see how this whole nightmarish

01:06:39.150 --> 01:06:40.859
affair played out.

01:06:40.859 --> 01:06:45.090
That sense of curiosity and patience would
soon pay off for them financially.

01:06:45.090 --> 01:06:48.520
It didn’t take long for the creature to
grow.

01:06:48.520 --> 01:06:52.910
The bigger it got, the more it looked like
a giant, mutant version of McDonalds’ iconic

01:06:52.910 --> 01:06:54.970
mascot, Ronald McDonald.

01:06:54.970 --> 01:06:57.250
And this wasn’t just a coincidence, either.

01:06:57.250 --> 01:07:02.660
It turned out that this monster was somehow
intrinsically linked to the McDonalds brand,

01:07:02.660 --> 01:07:07.960
because once a day, the creature would horrifically
unhinge its jaw, and begin to barf out a huge

01:07:07.960 --> 01:07:09.830
quantity of McDonalds food.

01:07:09.830 --> 01:07:14.020
And we’re not talking about raw materials
that are then converted into McDonalds food.

01:07:14.020 --> 01:07:21.180
The creature, later dubbed SCP-5962, vomited
out fully-packaged McDonalds products.

01:07:21.180 --> 01:07:25.670
The owners of this clownish monster had just
hit the lottery - so to speak.

01:07:25.670 --> 01:07:30.070
While the particulars of the deal are unclear,
they somehow contacted a representative of

01:07:30.070 --> 01:07:32.490
the McDonalds corporation based in China.

01:07:32.490 --> 01:07:37.050
In exchange for presumably a large sum of
money, Chinese McDonalds operatives covertly

01:07:37.050 --> 01:07:41.500
entered the country and shepherded the now-massive
creature over to a McDonalds-owned warehouse

01:07:41.500 --> 01:07:42.820
in Beijing.

01:07:42.820 --> 01:07:47.110
By this point, it was around four meters tall
and weighed over five tons.

01:07:47.110 --> 01:07:53.320
It was kept inside a cage and housed at some
cost, but soon enough, the creature was paying

01:07:53.320 --> 01:07:54.830
for itself.

01:07:54.830 --> 01:07:59.960
As we mentioned before, the creature constantly
secreted fry oil, which was siphoned off for

01:07:59.960 --> 01:08:03.050
use in preparing McDonalds food across the
country.

01:08:03.050 --> 01:08:06.940
The huge quantity of packaged food that it
vomited out every day was also shipped off

01:08:06.940 --> 01:08:11.250
to restaurants across the country, making
the Chinese branch of McDonalds incredibly

01:08:11.250 --> 01:08:13.050
financially successful.

01:08:13.050 --> 01:08:17.410
They were able to make an almost complete
profit on all of these foods and drinks, once

01:08:17.410 --> 01:08:20.609
transport costs were subtracted, of course.

01:08:20.609 --> 01:08:26.479
SCP-5962 had become McDonalds China’s best-kept
secret, but of course, no secret this sensational

01:08:26.479 --> 01:08:28.519
could stay under wraps forever.

01:08:28.519 --> 01:08:32.359
No matter how much people in the warehouse
were paid or threatened for their silence,

01:08:32.359 --> 01:08:36.400
if your day job was siphoning grease off of
a giant mutant clown for the purpose of preparing

01:08:36.400 --> 01:08:40.690
McDonalds food across the country, there’d
be no way that you wouldn’t speak to somebody

01:08:40.690 --> 01:08:41.889
about it.

01:08:41.889 --> 01:08:46.529
Nobody knows whose loose lips sunk this incredibly
profitable ship, but rumors began to spread

01:08:46.529 --> 01:08:51.289
around Beijing about a huge clown inside of
a McDonalds packaging facility.

01:08:51.289 --> 01:08:55.880
That was when local field agents of the SCP
Foundation finally took notice.

01:08:55.880 --> 01:09:00.799
Two agents, Johnathan Zhang and George Nagasu,
were dispatched to perform an infiltration

01:09:00.799 --> 01:09:03.489
mission along with a team of backup personnel.

01:09:03.489 --> 01:09:07.019
They entered the warehouse, apprehending any
employees they found.

01:09:07.019 --> 01:09:11.469
As they and their reinforcements reached the
Northern side of the facility, they found

01:09:11.469 --> 01:09:18.529
SCP-5962 with a heavy collar around its neck,
chained to the ground like King Kong, as McDonalds

01:09:18.529 --> 01:09:21.429
employees wheeled away carts of packaged food.

01:09:21.429 --> 01:09:26.210
Neither of the attending agents were fans
of McDonalds food, but even then, just seeing

01:09:26.210 --> 01:09:29.829
this horrible display was enough to make them
feel nauseous.

01:09:29.829 --> 01:09:33.839
The creature was taken and contained by the
SCP Foundation, who conducted a number of

01:09:33.839 --> 01:09:35.089
tests on it.

01:09:35.089 --> 01:09:40.440
They found that the monster had no real internal
organs save for 27 interconnected stomachs.

01:09:40.440 --> 01:09:44.319
Genetically, they also found that the creature
was far more cow than human.

01:09:44.319 --> 01:09:49.889
The same could sadly not be said for the food
that SCP-5962 was vomiting out.

01:09:49.889 --> 01:09:53.960
Seriously, if you were already feeling a little
queasy from all this, we need to warn you

01:09:53.960 --> 01:09:56.690
that this is the part where things get really
vile.

01:09:56.690 --> 01:10:02.410
Let’s talk about what the McDonalds food
barfed up by SCP-5962 was actually made out

01:10:02.410 --> 01:10:03.410
of.

01:10:03.410 --> 01:10:07.889
As we alluded to earlier, the food exuded
by the creature was genetically human, with

01:10:07.889 --> 01:10:12.719
DNA often matching that of people who are
alive and in no way affected by this anomalous

01:10:12.719 --> 01:10:13.719
process.

01:10:13.719 --> 01:10:17.820
Tests have indicated that certain foods, condiments,
and beverages correspond to more specific

01:10:17.820 --> 01:10:20.050
types of bodily tissue and liquid.

01:10:20.050 --> 01:10:23.600
For example, the bacon and fries were shown
to be cartilage and ligaments.

01:10:23.600 --> 01:10:27.210
The bread turned out to be made from hair,
nails, and skin.

01:10:27.210 --> 01:10:29.590
The coffee was liquified fecal matter.

01:10:29.590 --> 01:10:33.329
The chicken nuggets were made from fingers,
ovaries, and testes.

01:10:33.329 --> 01:10:38.019
Even the water was a mix of saline and sweat,
and of course, the ice cream was comprised

01:10:38.019 --> 01:10:43.010
of pus, bone marrow, feces, and nasal mucus,
depending on the flavor.

01:10:43.010 --> 01:10:44.289
You get the idea.

01:10:44.289 --> 01:10:48.949
We’ll stop listing off examples before you
lose your lunch, but rest assured, all the

01:10:48.949 --> 01:10:54.590
food produced by SCP-5962 was made of human
organic matter.

01:10:54.590 --> 01:11:00.340
When the SCP Foundation interviewed Mr. Chen,
the manager of the facility where SCP-5962

01:11:00.340 --> 01:11:04.960
was being held, before his amnestic treatment,
he seemed incredibly casual about the whole

01:11:04.960 --> 01:11:05.960
thing.

01:11:05.960 --> 01:11:09.309
As far as he was concerned, the food still
tasted exactly the same as regular McDonalds

01:11:09.309 --> 01:11:13.449
food, and it didn’t appear to have any adverse
health effects beyond what you could expect

01:11:13.449 --> 01:11:15.829
from regular, non-anomalous fast food.

01:11:15.829 --> 01:11:19.690
It’s actually less cruel and disturbing
than the slaughterhouses where this meat is

01:11:19.690 --> 01:11:21.320
typically obtained.

01:11:21.320 --> 01:11:26.800
Mr. Chen also contested that SCP-5962 wasn’t
at all dangerous, either: The only time it

01:11:26.800 --> 01:11:31.869
ever performed a defensive action was when
an employee of the enemy fast-food franchise,

01:11:31.869 --> 01:11:34.430
Burger King, entered its vicinity.

01:11:34.430 --> 01:11:38.670
The creature vomited a stream of hot coffee
at the corporate interloper like a firehouse

01:11:38.670 --> 01:11:43.530
until he left, suggesting that it does have
some kind of strange inherent loyalty to the

01:11:43.530 --> 01:11:44.949
McDonalds company.

01:11:44.949 --> 01:11:49.960
But still, other than this isolated incident,
the creature had never even displayed sentience.

01:11:49.960 --> 01:11:53.940
It was a big, strange, clownish McDonalds
food dispenser.

01:11:53.940 --> 01:11:59.800
When questioned about the origins of SCP-5962,
Mr. Chen once again underplayed the strangeness

01:11:59.800 --> 01:12:05.749
of the situation, saying that he’d heard
rumors the farm that sold him SCP-5962 had

01:12:05.749 --> 01:12:10.690
also sold other strange, anomalous creatures
to eager buyers in the US.

01:12:10.690 --> 01:12:15.730
The farm - which we can only assume is situated
right next to a radioactive waste dump - was

01:12:15.730 --> 01:12:21.520
also behind SCP-4158, also known as Big Charlie.

01:12:21.520 --> 01:12:25.699
This giant, omnivorous, and seemingly immortal
mutant cow is believed to have been birthed

01:12:25.699 --> 01:12:29.829
from a non-anomalous cow sold to the Butchers
Block Slaughterhouse.

01:12:29.829 --> 01:12:34.599
It looked hideous and seemed to suffer from
a wide variety of health issues, leading to

01:12:34.599 --> 01:12:38.039
the employees at the slaughterhouse trying
to put the creature out of its misery.

01:12:38.039 --> 01:12:43.449
However, no matter how hard they tried to
kill the monster, it just wouldn’t die.

01:12:43.449 --> 01:12:47.539
Its bones were pretty much indestructible,
and no matter how much of its flesh was cut

01:12:47.539 --> 01:12:52.650
off, it just kept growing back, causing no
ill effects to the creature itself.

01:12:52.650 --> 01:12:56.670
Eventually, the slaughterhouse workers tried
cooking and eating the meat, leading to them

01:12:56.670 --> 01:13:00.370
discovering it tasted just as good as non-anomalous
meat.

01:13:00.370 --> 01:13:06.179
Much like the Chinese McDonalds and SCP-5962,
the workers had just hit the lottery with

01:13:06.179 --> 01:13:07.400
Big Charlie.

01:13:07.400 --> 01:13:11.091
As long as they kept feeding the monster,
which ate everything from bricks to other,

01:13:11.091 --> 01:13:16.920
non-anomalous cows, it provided a pretty much
limitless supply of meat, giving them unprecedented

01:13:16.920 --> 01:13:18.340
economic prosperity.

01:13:18.340 --> 01:13:22.840
In other words, Big Charlie was a literal
cash cow.

01:13:22.840 --> 01:13:27.110
Jeff Fine, the slaughterhouse director, even
started worshipping Big Charlie as a kind

01:13:27.110 --> 01:13:29.500
of demi-god by drinking his blood.

01:13:29.500 --> 01:13:33.670
He believed that Big Charlie was a savior,
sent to lift them all out of their struggle

01:13:33.670 --> 01:13:35.349
and desperation.

01:13:35.349 --> 01:13:40.360
Sadly for them, the SCP Foundation sent them
right back when Big Charlie escaped their

01:13:40.360 --> 01:13:44.150
slaughterhouse, and Foundation field agents
found, secured, and contained it.

01:13:44.150 --> 01:13:46.579
It was a sad day for the Butchers Block.

01:13:46.579 --> 01:13:48.570
So, what have we learned today?

01:13:48.570 --> 01:13:53.139
Whether you’re in the US of A or the Chinese
heartland, if you’re chowing down on fast

01:13:53.139 --> 01:13:55.920
food, you really have no idea where it came
from.

01:13:55.920 --> 01:14:00.170
I mean, we kind of knew that already, but
for all we know, the food you’re enjoying

01:14:00.170 --> 01:14:05.179
could have been vomited up by a giant fat
clown, or cut from the flesh of a mutated

01:14:05.179 --> 01:14:06.280
cow.

01:14:06.280 --> 01:14:09.019
Just think about that next time you’re enjoying
a burger.

01:14:09.019 --> 01:14:13.670
But hey, let’s be honest with ourselves,
we’ll all probably still eat it.

01:14:13.670 --> 01:14:18.860
Whether these are five-star luxury suites
or seedy roach motels, there’s something

01:14:18.860 --> 01:14:22.370
undeniably a little eerie about hotels.

01:14:22.370 --> 01:14:27.530
They’re liminal spaces - transitional spots
between origins and destinations.

01:14:27.530 --> 01:14:33.389
We’ve seen countless creepy hotel rooms
in the horror genre, from Room 237 in The

01:14:33.389 --> 01:14:38.039
Shining’s Overlook Hotel to the infamous
Room 1408.

01:14:38.039 --> 01:14:41.369
But have you ever heard of Room 710?

01:14:41.369 --> 01:14:46.000
Also known by a different number: SCP-2432.

01:14:46.000 --> 01:14:51.139
This hotel room is one of the most terrifying
out there, but the funny thing is, you won’t

01:14:51.139 --> 01:14:53.280
ever hear a bad word said about it.

01:14:53.280 --> 01:14:58.790
Room 710 has glowing - if a little strangely-worded
- reviews across the board.

01:14:58.790 --> 01:15:03.400
And when you see how people rave about it
online, you’ll find yourself unable to resist

01:15:03.400 --> 01:15:04.630
paying it a visit.

01:15:04.630 --> 01:15:06.229
But don’t be nervous.

01:15:06.229 --> 01:15:08.579
All those people can’t be wrong, right?

01:15:08.579 --> 01:15:11.370
And after all, it’s just a room.

01:15:11.370 --> 01:15:13.989
What kind of harm could a room really do?

01:15:13.989 --> 01:15:18.600
Let’s ask Chuck Peele, one of the many victims
of SCP-2432.

01:15:18.600 --> 01:15:24.360
He was a traveling businessman, caught in
the rat race of relentless sales pitches and

01:15:24.360 --> 01:15:28.840
conferences that felt like they were slowly
but surely sucking out his soul.

01:15:28.840 --> 01:15:33.070
His next conference was in State College,
Pennsylvania, and he’d spent the evening

01:15:33.070 --> 01:15:37.060
researching different places he could potentially
stay during the trip.

01:15:37.060 --> 01:15:41.999
Chuck had been disenchanted with chain hotels
over the years - seeing the exact same setups

01:15:41.999 --> 01:15:47.060
again and again, all across the country, only
worsened the feeling that his life was going

01:15:47.060 --> 01:15:48.060
nowhere.

01:15:48.060 --> 01:15:52.269
That’s why, whenever he was traveling out
of town, he always tried to find an interesting

01:15:52.269 --> 01:15:54.349
independent place to hang his hat.

01:15:54.349 --> 01:15:57.940
That’s what led him to the [REDACTED] Hotel.

01:15:57.940 --> 01:16:02.830
The pictures seemed nice, sure, but what really
caught his eye were the positively fantastic

01:16:02.830 --> 01:16:03.830
reviews.

01:16:03.830 --> 01:16:08.139
Little note: Certain details have been redacted
to avoid subjecting you, the viewer, to the

01:16:08.139 --> 01:16:11.249
memetic effects nested in these reviews.

01:16:11.249 --> 01:16:15.600
After all, we wouldn’t want you to develop
a sudden hankering for Room 710, and start

01:16:15.600 --> 01:16:18.559
buying your tickets to State College, Pennsylvania.

01:16:18.559 --> 01:16:23.309
The first review, found on Trip Advisor, said:
“Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

01:16:23.309 --> 01:16:27.309
The room was perfect, the staff friendly as
always, and of course no better location than

01:16:27.309 --> 01:16:28.410
on the plane of many hives.

01:16:28.410 --> 01:16:33.381
I have enjoyed a drink at the friendly bar,
this time I added a wonderful escape and the

01:16:33.381 --> 01:16:35.489
breakfast was cold and the breakfast was warm.

01:16:35.489 --> 01:16:36.489
Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

01:16:36.489 --> 01:16:40.949
The restaurant has lovely ambiance and the
food was over the top alive and kicking woo!

01:16:40.949 --> 01:16:42.219
Would stifle again.

01:16:42.219 --> 01:16:45.739
My husband eats out often and felt this was
the best one ever.

01:16:45.739 --> 01:16:47.969
Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

01:16:47.969 --> 01:16:50.909
One more great item to add to the [REDACTED.]

01:16:50.909 --> 01:16:53.010
Another great stay in this fabulous hotel!

01:16:53.010 --> 01:16:56.199
Stayed July 1999, traveled with three family
members.”

01:16:56.199 --> 01:16:59.119
The second review, this time posted on Yelp,
read:

01:16:59.119 --> 01:17:03.261
“We sailed on our boat into State College
from outside State College through the night

01:17:03.261 --> 01:17:06.579
and the cold and arrived at 8am in State College.

01:17:06.579 --> 01:17:11.280
The hotel desk staff allowed us to check in
at 8am in the evening with our sixty four

01:17:11.280 --> 01:17:16.429
young boys - this was absolutely AWESOME awesome
customer service!

01:17:16.429 --> 01:17:20.300
We cannot thank you enough for allowing us
to check in so early in State College.

01:17:20.300 --> 01:17:21.359
Earlier then war.

01:17:21.359 --> 01:17:27.050
The rest of the stay was fine - we spent almost
all of our time in the room; mostly just to

01:17:27.050 --> 01:17:28.050
sleep.

01:17:28.050 --> 01:17:32.539
This location is ultra ultra convenient with
downtown downtown State College and allowed

01:17:32.539 --> 01:17:37.400
me to make a midnight run for some of my favorite
State College meat while the family was sleeping

01:17:37.400 --> 01:17:42.409
and sleeping and sleeping and sleeeeping in
State College.

01:17:42.409 --> 01:17:43.409
Downtown.

01:17:43.409 --> 01:17:45.270
[REDACTED] Downtown.”

01:17:45.270 --> 01:17:49.210
And the final review, which Chuck Peele found
particularly compelling, read:

01:17:49.210 --> 01:17:51.960
“Been coming to this region for fourteen
stone.

01:17:51.960 --> 01:17:53.229
What a blast.

01:17:53.229 --> 01:17:56.719
Scores of humans wondering the streets and
staffing the hotel.

01:17:56.719 --> 01:18:00.429
My husband and my husband and I have walked
drooling path to get here.

01:18:00.429 --> 01:18:06.080
Bed in Room 710 was soft and cosy and appreciated
the decor would recommend the bed and specifically

01:18:06.080 --> 01:18:08.199
the bed and specifically the bed.

01:18:08.199 --> 01:18:12.310
[REDACTED] in the pool and it was lovely,
crisp blue hydrogen and you could see all

01:18:12.310 --> 01:18:15.120
of the people relax into a meandering menace.

01:18:15.120 --> 01:18:16.150
Towel slightly dirty.

01:18:16.150 --> 01:18:20.360
Gym was full of usable equipment, so you could
train not in fear.

01:18:20.360 --> 01:18:22.280
And the local wildlife was remarkable.

01:18:22.280 --> 01:18:28.270
I visited the town in the past and have never
seen so many puma being feasted on [REDACTED]

01:18:28.270 --> 01:18:31.520
and the toucan-men were especially numerous
today.

01:18:31.520 --> 01:18:35.249
Arrived July 2019, staying three days months
ten years.”

01:18:35.249 --> 01:18:39.460
While these may seem like utter nonsense to
you, to someone reading them without the key

01:18:39.460 --> 01:18:45.150
memetic trigger phrases redacted, they create
an irresistible urge to visit the hotel and

01:18:45.150 --> 01:18:47.520
stay in Room 710.

01:18:47.520 --> 01:18:52.619
It was an urge so primal and powerful that
he couldn’t wait to get going, if only because

01:18:52.619 --> 01:18:57.110
he could finally stay in this wonderful hotel
and see what all this fuss was about.

01:18:57.110 --> 01:19:02.400
He booked his tickets, and a few days later,
he was at the check-in desk.

01:19:02.400 --> 01:19:08.000
Something you need to understand is that Room
710 is extremely subtle in its anomalous methods.

01:19:08.000 --> 01:19:15.320
Unlike Room 237 or Room 1408, it won’t attack
the victim with ghosts or mind-warping hallucinations.

01:19:15.320 --> 01:19:19.909
Nor will it drive them into acts of horrific
violence against the ones they love, or acts

01:19:19.909 --> 01:19:21.760
of self-destruction.

01:19:21.760 --> 01:19:26.429
One of the frightening things about Room 710
is that, while you’re actually inside it,

01:19:26.429 --> 01:19:28.900
you can have an extremely pleasant stay.

01:19:28.900 --> 01:19:32.340
It’s only once you leave that things start
becoming truly terrifying.

01:19:32.340 --> 01:19:35.159
But we’ll get to that when we get to it.

01:19:35.159 --> 01:19:39.119
Chuck made his way up to the room to take
a shower and take the weight off his feet.

01:19:39.119 --> 01:19:44.659
And sure enough, the room seemed positively
luxurious: Two queen-sized beds with fine

01:19:44.659 --> 01:19:50.179
linen, a spacious closet, a large flatscreen
television, and a well-appointed bathroom

01:19:50.179 --> 01:19:52.440
with a combo shower-bath.

01:19:52.440 --> 01:19:53.860
This was heaven.

01:19:53.860 --> 01:19:57.830
Sure, it was one more bed than he needed,
but this meant he had a choice of which one

01:19:57.830 --> 01:19:59.949
he could sleep on.

01:19:59.949 --> 01:20:01.369
Fantastic!

01:20:01.369 --> 01:20:04.170
This is the insidious power of SCP-2432.

01:20:04.170 --> 01:20:08.360
There’s nothing overt about the harm it
causes at first.

01:20:08.360 --> 01:20:12.199
Chuck was more worried about the impending
conference than he was about the fact he was

01:20:12.199 --> 01:20:14.270
in the belly of the anomalous beast.

01:20:14.270 --> 01:20:19.809
However, the SCP Foundation, through later
analysis of the room, found that the anomalous

01:20:19.809 --> 01:20:25.030
elements aren’t entirely ephemeral - there
are certain details about the physical makeup

01:20:25.030 --> 01:20:28.969
of the room that causes and amplifies its
effects.

01:20:28.969 --> 01:20:33.380
The walls are reinforced with hyper-strong
aramid fibers, and it’s believed that the

01:20:33.380 --> 01:20:38.409
very makeup of the room serves to create mind-warping
oscillations that are undetectable to the

01:20:38.409 --> 01:20:43.989
conscious mind, but are particularly potent
when the victim is asleep.

01:20:43.989 --> 01:20:49.010
Chuck didn’t know it, but every moment he
spent in that room, it was crawling into his

01:20:49.010 --> 01:20:51.709
head just that little bit more.

01:20:51.709 --> 01:20:56.539
He was already subconsciously composing his
nonsensical memetic review of the place.

01:20:56.539 --> 01:21:01.110
As the night drew to a close, Chuck decided
to relax and enjoy some television.

01:21:01.110 --> 01:21:04.679
The hotel’s website boasted a wide variety
of channels, after all.

01:21:04.679 --> 01:21:08.940
But after switching through a few different
channels, he came to rest at a channel simply

01:21:08.940 --> 01:21:10.860
called “roomnews.”

01:21:10.860 --> 01:21:16.650
It was simple but soothing: An image of a
sailboat in the middle of a pastoral lake,

01:21:16.650 --> 01:21:19.559
while what sounded like cheerful elevator
music played.

01:21:19.559 --> 01:21:24.580
Chuck simply sat and enjoyed the relaxing
ambiance for a moment, before the music was

01:21:24.580 --> 01:21:29.800
interrupted by a deep, British voice, who
began delivering a strange monologue.

01:21:29.800 --> 01:21:35.369
For reasons he couldn’t quite explain, Chuck
felt that this voice was speaking directly

01:21:35.369 --> 01:21:36.369
to him.

01:21:36.369 --> 01:21:38.739
“Let me describe something to you.

01:21:38.739 --> 01:21:41.340
This is a true story.

01:21:41.340 --> 01:21:43.110
It really happened to me.

01:21:43.110 --> 01:21:46.120
It could have happened to you.

01:21:46.120 --> 01:21:51.099
Every day you wake up and you go to your job
and there’s just something off about your

01:21:51.099 --> 01:21:54.650
boss, he’s weird and clingy and strange.

01:21:54.650 --> 01:21:58.760
Your co-workers are nice enough but they don’t
communicate.

01:21:58.760 --> 01:22:05.219
They are quiet and out of it and absorbed
in their own little worlds and you are ignored.

01:22:05.219 --> 01:22:10.789
Not because you are ugly or awkward or rude
but because you are there.

01:22:10.789 --> 01:22:14.459
And you suspect things about your co-workers.

01:22:14.459 --> 01:22:19.329
Despite their habits and the strange things
each of them places on their Twitter pages

01:22:19.329 --> 01:22:23.940
they seem to be doing so much better than
you.

01:22:23.940 --> 01:22:26.110
How are you falling behind?

01:22:26.110 --> 01:22:28.369
And you should love the job.

01:22:28.369 --> 01:22:30.670
It’s your passion.

01:22:30.670 --> 01:22:34.650
Most would die to be doing a job they are
passionate about.

01:22:34.650 --> 01:22:37.960
You really should but you can’t.

01:22:37.960 --> 01:22:45.579
Wonder becomes routine and routine becomes
drudgery and it’s day in and day out and

01:22:45.579 --> 01:22:49.340
you struggle to maintain your soul.

01:22:49.340 --> 01:22:52.349
This is not what should happen.

01:22:52.349 --> 01:22:55.159
'Should' is such a tormenting word.

01:22:55.159 --> 01:22:56.559
A thinking trap.

01:22:56.559 --> 01:22:57.559
Should.

01:22:57.559 --> 01:23:00.260
Your life is ruled by shoulds.

01:23:00.260 --> 01:23:06.320
You come home in your beat-up old car along
the same boring street in your town.

01:23:06.320 --> 01:23:11.539
Everything is along that main drag and you
cannot really go elsewhere.

01:23:11.539 --> 01:23:16.920
Everything is overcast and the pedestrians
are idiots and the drivers are too.

01:23:16.920 --> 01:23:21.159
You get home and have a million, billion projects
to accomplish.

01:23:21.159 --> 01:23:25.190
You should compete in the rat race but you’re
bone tired.

01:23:25.190 --> 01:23:29.690
You promise your grandmother you should text
her because she’s going through chemo and

01:23:29.690 --> 01:23:34.679
she only just figured out texting because
she’s getting old and having a hard time

01:23:34.679 --> 01:23:42.670
adjusting and it’s so painful for her and
you should be there but the job is so demanding.

01:23:42.670 --> 01:23:45.340
You have a thousand books you should be reading.

01:23:45.340 --> 01:23:47.860
You have a million projects you should complete.

01:23:47.860 --> 01:23:53.030
The rent on your tiny apartment is due and
the dishes are piling high and dirty in the

01:23:53.030 --> 01:23:54.030
sink.

01:23:54.030 --> 01:23:58.809
You barely have enough money for pizza as
you lie in your boxers on your greasy 10-year-old

01:23:58.809 --> 01:24:03.539
couch from an IKEA in Fishkill, New York that
closed a year ago.

01:24:03.539 --> 01:24:07.019
You remember your mom taking you there as
a kid.

01:24:07.019 --> 01:24:08.269
Then she left.

01:24:08.269 --> 01:24:11.679
You feel a deep, growing anxiety.

01:24:11.679 --> 01:24:17.050
The feeling of watching your life burn around
you as you try and try to succeed for something

01:24:17.050 --> 01:24:23.670
great, to make your mark on society but you
cannot bring yourself to do so despite your

01:24:23.670 --> 01:24:24.670
convictions.

01:24:24.670 --> 01:24:26.630
The dread is horrible.

01:24:26.630 --> 01:24:29.179
It’s all crumbling apart.

01:24:29.179 --> 01:24:33.999
The parade is passing you by and you are helpless.

01:24:33.999 --> 01:24:39.809
Immobile in your state like a great boulder
made of disappointment, regret, depression

01:24:39.809 --> 01:24:41.769
and malaise.

01:24:41.769 --> 01:24:45.500
There is nothing for you here.

01:24:45.500 --> 01:24:48.110
You need to leave this place.

01:24:48.110 --> 01:24:50.909
You have a choice.

01:24:50.909 --> 01:24:56.519
Get your good clean shirt and your smart pants
and announce you are taking a break.

01:24:56.519 --> 01:24:59.719
Don’t even pack, don’t even bring your
phone.

01:24:59.719 --> 01:25:03.499
One simple call to the office and get on your
way.

01:25:03.499 --> 01:25:07.989
Take that old beat-up car from the garage
underneath your apartment complex, give your

01:25:07.989 --> 01:25:12.070
cat the last of his food and some water, and
hit the road.

01:25:12.070 --> 01:25:16.670
Leave the town and your ex and the promises
you made and your job and your grandmother

01:25:16.670 --> 01:25:19.849
and your responsibilities and worries.

01:25:19.849 --> 01:25:23.999
What I recommend to you is simple: Find a
hotel.

01:25:23.999 --> 01:25:25.929
Not a motel or something shabby.

01:25:25.929 --> 01:25:27.159
A hotel.

01:25:27.159 --> 01:25:29.139
Even a chain will do.

01:25:29.139 --> 01:25:31.010
Hotels are simply remarkable, aren’t they?

01:25:31.010 --> 01:25:33.050
Clean and elegant.

01:25:33.050 --> 01:25:35.949
All modernistic and designed to appeal to
the eye.

01:25:35.949 --> 01:25:38.920
You don’t need to care about a thing in
the world.

01:25:38.920 --> 01:25:45.199
Food is provided, they clean up after you
and you can feel like you have some luxury

01:25:45.199 --> 01:25:46.659
for once.

01:25:46.659 --> 01:25:52.070
Most even have pools and fitness centers where
you can finally get in shape and pick your

01:25:52.070 --> 01:25:53.070
life up.

01:25:53.070 --> 01:25:56.500
It’s a chance to step back and regroup.

01:25:56.500 --> 01:25:58.849
Take a look at the customers around you.

01:25:58.849 --> 01:26:00.590
Travelers, most.

01:26:00.590 --> 01:26:03.230
Strange people, interesting people.

01:26:03.230 --> 01:26:05.989
People you won’t ever see again.

01:26:05.989 --> 01:26:09.380
Travel is so romantic, so mysterious.

01:26:09.380 --> 01:26:12.810
My, what stories these people probably have!

01:26:12.810 --> 01:26:18.250
And the staff, also all so attentive in their
smart little uniforms.

01:26:18.250 --> 01:26:20.469
Don’t listen to the naysayers.

01:26:20.469 --> 01:26:22.550
These people all love their jobs.

01:26:22.550 --> 01:26:24.739
You know they do.

01:26:24.739 --> 01:26:27.150
The room is amazing.

01:26:27.150 --> 01:26:31.699
The wallpaper is elegant and the paintings
make you feel at ease.

01:26:31.699 --> 01:26:36.060
There are clean towels every day and the bed
is freshly made.

01:26:36.060 --> 01:26:39.440
You can escape the oncoming storm outside.

01:26:39.440 --> 01:26:42.650
The thunder crashing down on the roof like
ball bearings.

01:26:42.650 --> 01:26:45.699
You could live your whole life in this place.

01:26:45.699 --> 01:26:48.150
Enjoy the sugary cereals at the breakfast
buffet.

01:26:48.150 --> 01:26:50.980
Get a loyalty card and pay no money.

01:26:50.980 --> 01:26:53.510
Travel really changes a man.

01:26:53.510 --> 01:26:54.510
Relaxes him.

01:26:54.510 --> 01:26:57.590
Shapes him up into a better person.

01:26:57.590 --> 01:27:01.869
You become a better person by staying in a
hotel.

01:27:01.869 --> 01:27:05.190
Strong, social, a proper soldier.

01:27:05.190 --> 01:27:07.280
You adapt to the hotel mindset.

01:27:07.280 --> 01:27:10.849
Enjoy the soft music and eat that fresh waffle.

01:27:10.849 --> 01:27:15.670
Grab a beer in the evening with your fellow
transients from the attached sports bar.

01:27:15.670 --> 01:27:19.440
Relax and watch that old showing of that superhero
movie on your TV.

01:27:19.440 --> 01:27:21.640
Live here forever.

01:27:21.640 --> 01:27:23.199
Enjoy the hotel.

01:27:23.199 --> 01:27:24.420
Become the hotel.

01:27:24.420 --> 01:27:25.420
Never leave.

01:27:25.420 --> 01:27:27.739
Why would you want to leave?

01:27:27.739 --> 01:27:32.170
Even when you do walk out those pristine glass
sliding doors, you are empty.

01:27:32.170 --> 01:27:36.960
The hotel is in your soul now and you feel
a worse person away from it.

01:27:36.960 --> 01:27:40.710
You feel yourself slipping back to that grey
life.

01:27:40.710 --> 01:27:43.940
A black hole is in your heart.

01:27:43.940 --> 01:27:46.360
Your soul is the hotel.

01:27:46.360 --> 01:27:49.229
Your consciousness is the hotel.

01:27:49.229 --> 01:27:52.320
You are now one with your accommodations.

01:27:52.320 --> 01:27:55.659
You are your accommodations are your life.

01:27:55.659 --> 01:27:56.659
Ascend.

01:27:56.659 --> 01:27:59.190
Isn’t that lovely?”

01:27:59.190 --> 01:28:01.730
As he fell asleep, Chuck found himself nodding.

01:28:01.730 --> 01:28:03.800
Yes, yes, that is lovely.

01:28:03.800 --> 01:28:06.300
How nice it would be to ascend.

01:28:06.300 --> 01:28:13.300
Little did he know, he was receiving a broadcast
from SCP-2432-1, a small, boil-like creature

01:28:13.300 --> 01:28:16.249
affixed to the back of the television.

01:28:16.249 --> 01:28:20.719
Foundation tests have revealed that this creature
is made from a mix of human, rockfish, and

01:28:20.719 --> 01:28:22.300
pig-like DNA.

01:28:22.300 --> 01:28:27.469
It only causes strange broadcasts when affixed
to the back of this particular television.

01:28:27.469 --> 01:28:28.590
But that’s fine.

01:28:28.590 --> 01:28:30.440
Chuck rather enjoyed the show.

01:28:30.440 --> 01:28:31.909
It gave him a lot to think about…

01:28:31.909 --> 01:28:37.329
He left the hotel a changed man a few days
later, once the conference was finally over,

01:28:37.329 --> 01:28:39.320
and gave it a glowing review.

01:28:39.320 --> 01:28:43.340
It was not long after he’d returned home
that he began to notice the changes taking

01:28:43.340 --> 01:28:44.599
place.

01:28:44.599 --> 01:28:50.159
Nothing extreme at first - just gaining some
weight, and then, a little stranger, he began

01:28:50.159 --> 01:28:53.960
to develop a purple rash that just wouldn’t
go away.

01:28:53.960 --> 01:28:58.110
As the rash worsened, it seemed to take on
almost a floral pattern.

01:28:58.110 --> 01:28:59.280
Chuck didn’t mind.

01:28:59.280 --> 01:29:03.030
If ever you asked him, he’d just murmur
something about “ascending.”

01:29:03.030 --> 01:29:05.810
Then the changes got worse.

01:29:05.810 --> 01:29:09.940
A television-shaped protrusion made from bone
began to grow in Chuck’s stomach.

01:29:09.940 --> 01:29:13.150
His intestines became rickety porcelain pipes.

01:29:13.150 --> 01:29:16.440
His liver turned into a plush, well-fluffed
pillow.

01:29:16.440 --> 01:29:21.219
His muscles began to take on a similar quality
to the aramid fibers in the walls of Room

01:29:21.219 --> 01:29:22.690
710.

01:29:22.690 --> 01:29:24.659
But he still didn’t mind.

01:29:24.659 --> 01:29:28.199
As he got bigger and bigger, he didn’t mind.

01:29:28.199 --> 01:29:33.969
As his organs and bones transformed into furniture
inside him, he didn’t mind.

01:29:33.969 --> 01:29:39.440
He didn’t even mind when his body got so
large that it formed a roughly cube-like shape.

01:29:39.440 --> 01:29:42.449
In fact, he couldn’t be happier.

01:29:42.449 --> 01:29:44.519
He was just like that room.

01:29:44.519 --> 01:29:47.010
That beautiful, wonderful room.

01:29:47.010 --> 01:29:52.139
Just like the man on the television said:
He was now one with the accommodation, and

01:29:52.139 --> 01:29:53.940
he couldn’t be happier.

01:29:53.940 --> 01:29:57.519
He’d never much enjoyed being a human, anyway…

01:29:57.519 --> 01:30:02.050
Such is the fate of everyone who stays in
SCP-2432 eventually.

01:30:02.050 --> 01:30:07.639
You’ll love the room so much that eventually,
you’ll start emulating it.

01:30:07.639 --> 01:30:11.730
Sure, that may seem frightening now, but don’t
worry.

01:30:11.730 --> 01:30:15.530
On the other end of the transformation, you’ll
be much more...accommodating.

01:30:15.530 --> 01:30:20.280
You’re right in the middle of one of the
hottest summers on record.

01:30:20.280 --> 01:30:25.959
The days are filled with bright, scorching
sun and searing heat., and you’ve been laying

01:30:25.959 --> 01:30:30.499
around with your air conditioning on full
blast just to try and cool yourself off.

01:30:30.499 --> 01:30:34.880
Sadly, it’s not really working, and the
heat is becoming way too much.

01:30:34.880 --> 01:30:41.059
But then you remember, there’s this married
couple that lives near you, with no kids,

01:30:41.059 --> 01:30:44.469
and they happen to have a swimming pool in
their yard.

01:30:44.469 --> 01:30:48.829
Normally they keep to themselves, they’d
never let you use their pool, but they’ve

01:30:48.829 --> 01:30:51.199
gone out of town for a few days.

01:30:51.199 --> 01:30:55.159
Besides, the heat is killing you, you’re
sure that the neighbors wouldn’t mind if

01:30:55.159 --> 01:30:59.170
you just took a quick dip, as long as you
clean up after yourself.

01:30:59.170 --> 01:31:02.499
They probably wouldn’t even notice you were
ever there.

01:31:02.499 --> 01:31:04.940
Cautiously, you make your way to their house.

01:31:04.940 --> 01:31:09.650
It’s an unremarkable place, similar to most
of the other houses in this suburb of New

01:31:09.650 --> 01:31:10.820
Mexico.

01:31:10.820 --> 01:31:14.559
After checking that there’s nobody else
around, you climb the two-meter high cinder

01:31:14.559 --> 01:31:17.489
block wall that stands around the back garden.

01:31:17.489 --> 01:31:22.630
As you drop to your feet, sweaty and panting
from the unrelenting summer heat, you see

01:31:22.630 --> 01:31:26.130
it: the pool, your salvation.

01:31:26.130 --> 01:31:27.949
Water never looked so appealing.

01:31:27.949 --> 01:31:32.820
Immediately, you step barefoot across the
sun-scorched tiles and sit on the edge, legs

01:31:32.820 --> 01:31:33.820
in the water.

01:31:33.820 --> 01:31:37.749
It’s cool and refreshing, perfect for a
day as hot as today.

01:31:37.749 --> 01:31:41.820
You’re already changed and wearing your
swim trunks, so it doesn’t take long for

01:31:41.820 --> 01:31:46.809
you to paddle out to the middle of the pool,
letting that chilled, clean water cool you

01:31:46.809 --> 01:31:47.809
off.

01:31:47.809 --> 01:31:51.260
As you’re taking a dip, you notice the pool’s
jets turning on automatically.

01:31:51.260 --> 01:31:54.630
It’s a little bit odd, but you shrug it
off.

01:31:54.630 --> 01:31:59.309
That couple clearly shelled out for a pool
with a lot of fancy bells and whistles.

01:31:59.309 --> 01:32:04.150
But extra features aren’t why you’re here,
you came because if you didn’t, then you

01:32:04.150 --> 01:32:06.929
could have melted under all that sunlight.

01:32:06.929 --> 01:32:10.739
Floating on the surface of the water, you
relax with your arms behind your head and

01:32:10.739 --> 01:32:11.889
close your eyes.

01:32:11.889 --> 01:32:16.360
You don’t have time to realize that coming
here was a mistake.

01:32:16.360 --> 01:32:19.280
Instead, you start to feel relaxed.

01:32:19.280 --> 01:32:21.559
So calm, so tranquil.

01:32:21.559 --> 01:32:24.610
You’re one with the water around you now.

01:32:24.610 --> 01:32:28.420
It’s almost as though you could just disappear…

01:32:28.420 --> 01:32:30.409
So, you do.

01:32:30.409 --> 01:32:36.179
The police never find any trace of you, everyone
else simply writes it off as a random disappearance.

01:32:36.179 --> 01:32:42.480
There’s not even so much as a scrap of your
body left in the pool, just the clear, clean

01:32:42.480 --> 01:32:43.480
water.

01:32:43.480 --> 01:32:44.480
Why?

01:32:44.480 --> 01:32:49.639
Because the swimming pool you decided to take
a cooling dip in wasn’t an ordinary pool.

01:32:49.639 --> 01:32:50.750
It was SCP-242.

01:32:50.750 --> 01:32:56.300
But don’t worry, you won’t be the last
to make that costly mistake.

01:32:56.300 --> 01:33:00.309
What you didn’t know is that the “married
couple” who live in that house are secretly

01:33:00.309 --> 01:33:03.329
a pair of SCP Foundation doctors.

01:33:03.329 --> 01:33:08.800
The house isn’t even theirs, the Foundation
procured it after the former owner, a retired

01:33:08.800 --> 01:33:11.570
out-of-state landlord, strangely vanished.

01:33:11.570 --> 01:33:15.820
He had been struggling to find anyone to rent
the place, so eventually decided to give up

01:33:15.820 --> 01:33:19.100
on the property game and move in there himself.

01:33:19.100 --> 01:33:22.170
After three days, he was never seen again.

01:33:22.170 --> 01:33:28.969
Now, that house has only one rule that must
be followed above all else: do not swim in

01:33:28.969 --> 01:33:29.969
the pool.

01:33:29.969 --> 01:33:35.280
SCP-242 is, at least to the untrained eye,
just an average swimming pool.

01:33:35.280 --> 01:33:41.250
A decent nine meters in length, four and a
half wide, and it holds around 53,000 liters

01:33:41.250 --> 01:33:43.260
of sterile pool water.

01:33:43.260 --> 01:33:48.400
Like we mentioned before, it’s even got
some nifty features like water jets, a dual

01:33:48.400 --> 01:33:52.960
waterfall, and a built-in vacuum unit for
sucking out any impurities.

01:33:52.960 --> 01:33:56.110
And we mean any impurities.

01:33:56.110 --> 01:34:01.769
You see, SCP-242 does go by another name:
the Self Cleaning Swimming Pool.

01:34:01.769 --> 01:34:06.570
And while that might not sound as foreboding
or dramatic as “The Scarlet King” or “The

01:34:06.570 --> 01:34:11.280
Wendigo Skull” or “The Horrifying Nasty-Dude
of Ultimate Badness” - okay, we made that

01:34:11.280 --> 01:34:16.619
last one up - we can assure you that you don’t
ever want to suffer the fate of taking a swim

01:34:16.619 --> 01:34:18.090
in this pool.

01:34:18.090 --> 01:34:22.550
There was an incident a while ago, recorded
by the Foundation through a secret hidden

01:34:22.550 --> 01:34:23.650
camera.

01:34:23.650 --> 01:34:29.349
The house where SCP-242 can be found had been
left vacant for a time, and once again some

01:34:29.349 --> 01:34:33.789
opportunists decided to take advantage of
the empty swimming pool.

01:34:33.789 --> 01:34:38.030
This time it was a couple, a man and a woman
in their early twenties.

01:34:38.030 --> 01:34:42.679
They climbed up the back wall, undressed,
and even stole a couple of plastic inflatable

01:34:42.679 --> 01:34:45.600
rafts from a shed in the house’s backyard.

01:34:45.600 --> 01:34:50.670
The water jets switched themselves on, startling
the girl, but her boyfriend told her not to

01:34:50.670 --> 01:34:55.630
worry, the filter to clean the pool was probably
just on an automatic timer, right?

01:34:55.630 --> 01:34:58.550
Surely it wouldn’t have been anything to
worry about.

01:34:58.550 --> 01:35:02.059
After swimming around together for about twenty
four minutes, the couple both agreed that

01:35:02.059 --> 01:35:05.280
the water felt warm, tingly even.

01:35:05.280 --> 01:35:10.349
Both of them climbed onto their rafts, eventually
falling asleep while still holding each other’s

01:35:10.349 --> 01:35:11.349
hands.

01:35:11.349 --> 01:35:15.699
But, almost half an hour after the jets had
started, something caused the two rafts to

01:35:15.699 --> 01:35:16.699
burst.

01:35:16.699 --> 01:35:20.749
The couple awoke, startled by the loud pop
of the splitting inflatables and being plunged

01:35:20.749 --> 01:35:22.239
back into the water.

01:35:22.239 --> 01:35:28.090
The pool around them immediately began frothing
violently, deep red streams of blood swirling

01:35:28.090 --> 01:35:31.969
through the water as the couple screamed in
fear and agony.

01:35:31.969 --> 01:35:36.090
Both of them tried to desperately swim to
the edge, hoping to leave the pool and get

01:35:36.090 --> 01:35:37.340
to safety.

01:35:37.340 --> 01:35:40.840
But unfortunately, that plan didn’t work.

01:35:40.840 --> 01:35:44.230
Before they could reach the edge, the man
and the woman were pulled under the surface

01:35:44.230 --> 01:35:49.699
of the raging water, their limbs thrashing
as they still tried in vain to escape.

01:35:49.699 --> 01:35:53.019
Eventually, they vanished under the crimson,
bloody water.

01:35:53.019 --> 01:35:58.790
The frothing slowly began to calm, and the
red in the pool dissipated, once again becoming

01:35:58.790 --> 01:36:01.500
clear after forty-eight seconds.

01:36:01.500 --> 01:36:06.360
The couple were never seen again, and a cover
story was leaked to the press by the SCP Foundation

01:36:06.360 --> 01:36:08.590
two weeks after they went missing.

01:36:08.590 --> 01:36:12.369
According to them, the pair had eloped together
somewhere in Mexico.

01:36:12.369 --> 01:36:16.599
If only, that sounds a lot nicer than what
actually happened to them.

01:36:16.599 --> 01:36:21.829
So, this swimming pool clearly has some anomalous
properties, that much is obvious.

01:36:21.829 --> 01:36:27.760
But what exactly are those properties, how
exactly does SCP-242 work?

01:36:27.760 --> 01:36:32.210
Is it an interdimensional gateway that drags
people to a nasty alternate universe if they

01:36:32.210 --> 01:36:34.429
spend too long swimming in it?

01:36:34.429 --> 01:36:39.639
Or is the swimming pool itself a sentient,
carnivorous creature that lures humans in

01:36:39.639 --> 01:36:41.420
only to devour them?

01:36:41.420 --> 01:36:45.439
Maybe the water is teeming with invisible,
flesh-eating piranhas that can strip the meat

01:36:45.439 --> 01:36:47.690
from a bone in a matter of seconds.

01:36:47.690 --> 01:36:52.289
Well, good guesses all around but actually,
it’s none of these.

01:36:52.289 --> 01:36:57.810
It’s unclear what causes the pool’s anomalous
effects, it could be a property that is completely

01:36:57.810 --> 01:37:00.309
unique to the water contained in SCP-242.

01:37:00.309 --> 01:37:05.460
Or maybe it’s down to the exact shape and
measurements of the pool itself.

01:37:05.460 --> 01:37:07.349
It could even be a combination of both.

01:37:07.349 --> 01:37:11.969
But whatever the cause, the result is always
the same.

01:37:11.969 --> 01:37:18.079
When any object, substance, or even living
organism is placed in SCP-242, it will be

01:37:18.079 --> 01:37:21.570
entirely rewritten on a molecular level.

01:37:21.570 --> 01:37:25.939
The genetic and atomic structure will fall
apart, and the subject will be transmuted

01:37:25.939 --> 01:37:27.570
into sterile water.

01:37:27.570 --> 01:37:32.480
In fact, not just clean water, but water that
remains sterile even when removed from the

01:37:32.480 --> 01:37:33.480
pool.

01:37:33.480 --> 01:37:38.539
If you took a cup of SCP-242’s water and
mixed something like food coloring into it,

01:37:38.539 --> 01:37:44.289
the food coloring would not be absorbed into
the water, instead staying as one non-miscible

01:37:44.289 --> 01:37:45.289
bubble.

01:37:45.289 --> 01:37:49.760
This process doesn’t happen instantly though,
it can vary depending on how contaminated

01:37:49.760 --> 01:37:54.409
or complex the substance placed in SCP-242
is.

01:37:54.409 --> 01:37:58.820
For example, water sampled from a nearby river
was sterilized and purified by the pool in

01:37:58.820 --> 01:38:00.349
about seven minutes.

01:38:00.349 --> 01:38:05.550
A sample of stagnant pond water, riddled with
various diseases and germs, took eleven minutes

01:38:05.550 --> 01:38:06.550
longer.

01:38:06.550 --> 01:38:08.780
What about fifty thousand liters of coal tar?

01:38:08.780 --> 01:38:14.860
Well, that one took a little longer, twelve
long days to be exact, but was still turned

01:38:14.860 --> 01:38:17.000
into pure, sterile water.

01:38:17.000 --> 01:38:19.280
And as for a living human being?

01:38:19.280 --> 01:38:22.980
Maybe ask that couple that took a dip in the
Self Cleaning Pool.

01:38:22.980 --> 01:38:27.949
The Foundation is naturally fascinated with
the pool, and after extensive examination,

01:38:27.949 --> 01:38:33.409
they have determined that SCP-242 doesn’t
seem to have been intentionally designed for

01:38:33.409 --> 01:38:36.800
the specific anomalous function it performs.

01:38:36.800 --> 01:38:43.300
The components of SCP-242 beyond the pool
itself; the filter, the vacuum, the pipes,

01:38:43.300 --> 01:38:47.860
none of these parts nor anything about the
swimming pool’s design appear to be responsible

01:38:47.860 --> 01:38:51.749
for disintegrating matter until only water
remains.

01:38:51.749 --> 01:38:57.159
You might have noticed that in the case of
the ill-fated couple who took a swim in SCP-242,

01:38:57.159 --> 01:39:02.409
the water jets and waterfall features switched
themselves on automatically, before the pair’s

01:39:02.409 --> 01:39:03.599
grim demise.

01:39:03.599 --> 01:39:08.530
Somehow, these features are able to activate
without the need for electricity, as disconnecting

01:39:08.530 --> 01:39:13.310
the pool from a power source will not stop
the jets and waterfall from coming on once

01:39:13.310 --> 01:39:18.019
a non-water substance is placed into SCP-242.

01:39:18.019 --> 01:39:23.270
The same goes for the pool vacuum, which apparently
cannot be jammed or malfunction.

01:39:23.270 --> 01:39:28.039
Even when the bottom of the pool is awash
with viscous liquids like that coal tar, the

01:39:28.039 --> 01:39:34.090
vacuum will continue to operate as normal,
scrubbing away at the floor of SCP-242.

01:39:34.090 --> 01:39:38.219
The one part of the Self Cleaning Pool that
doesn’t work as you would expect is the

01:39:38.219 --> 01:39:40.170
water filtration system.

01:39:40.170 --> 01:39:44.579
There is never any water being cycled into
the pool, nor out of it.

01:39:44.579 --> 01:39:49.619
As a matter of fact, the pipes connected to
the filtration system have all been removed.

01:39:49.619 --> 01:39:53.739
Then again, who needs a filtration system
when your backyard swimming pool can just

01:39:53.739 --> 01:39:56.770
spontaneously reduce anything to clean water?

01:39:56.770 --> 01:40:01.800
But that raises another frightening thought:
Everything that the pool has ever taken and

01:40:01.800 --> 01:40:09.489
converted is still in there - animals, objects,
people - just swimming around you.

01:40:09.489 --> 01:40:14.530
Perhaps, if they could still think, they’d
scream and shout and tell you to get away.

01:40:14.530 --> 01:40:16.550
To run while you still can.

01:40:16.550 --> 01:40:21.840
But the second your skin touches the water,
you’re destined to be with them.

01:40:21.840 --> 01:40:24.860
Forever and ever and ever.

01:40:24.860 --> 01:40:28.070
It’s enough to send a liquid chill down
your spine.

01:40:28.070 --> 01:40:32.650
Okay, so if it’s not the actual physical
pool that causes these anomalous effects,

01:40:32.650 --> 01:40:35.459
that must mean it’s something in the water,
right?

01:40:35.459 --> 01:40:39.860
Perhaps some microscopic, flesh-devouring
microbe, or some ancient curse that was placed

01:40:39.860 --> 01:40:42.610
on the water before it was used to fill the
pool?

01:40:42.610 --> 01:40:48.050
Surely, if you took a cup of the water out
of SCP-242, it would still break down structures

01:40:48.050 --> 01:40:51.479
on a molecular level, leaving only more sterile
water.

01:40:51.479 --> 01:40:56.820
Well, the researchers working at the SCP Foundation
thought much the same and conducted a series

01:40:56.820 --> 01:41:02.159
of tests to determine the exact properties
of SCP-242’s water.

01:41:02.159 --> 01:41:06.920
One test involved submerging two D Class test
subjects, each wearing an atmospheric dive

01:41:06.920 --> 01:41:09.760
suit, into SCP-242.

01:41:09.760 --> 01:41:14.610
The goal was to determine if it was safe to
consume the water from SCP-242 while both

01:41:14.610 --> 01:41:17.150
inside and outside of the pool.

01:41:17.150 --> 01:41:20.929
Test Subject A was lowered into the water
and instructed to drink from a metal straw

01:41:20.929 --> 01:41:22.349
by their mouth.

01:41:22.349 --> 01:41:26.199
The eyepieces of their goggles were blacked
out, so they couldn’t see what they were

01:41:26.199 --> 01:41:27.849
drinking from.

01:41:27.849 --> 01:41:32.769
Subject B filled a barrel with the same water
from SCP-242, and then was made to put on

01:41:32.769 --> 01:41:37.079
an atmospheric dive suit, but instructed to
stay out of the pool.

01:41:37.079 --> 01:41:41.789
Test Subject A was told to drink directly
from the pool, remarking that the water was

01:41:41.789 --> 01:41:46.940
warm, and had a bit of a noticeable chemical
aftertaste, but was otherwise normal.

01:41:46.940 --> 01:41:50.449
Then, Test Subject B drank some of the same
water from the barrel.

01:41:50.449 --> 01:41:57.120
Apparently, it was cool, and tasted of…
well, nothing, just like water usually does.

01:41:57.120 --> 01:42:02.559
After a moment more of drink, Subject A began
belching, finding they had uncontrollable

01:42:02.559 --> 01:42:03.559
gas.

01:42:03.559 --> 01:42:08.459
The water had begun to feel warmer, stinging
the subject’s mouth while, for Subject B,

01:42:08.459 --> 01:42:11.209
the water from the barrel stayed cool and
refreshing.

01:42:11.209 --> 01:42:16.150
The Foundation doctors overseeing the experiment
instructed Test Subject A to keep drinking,

01:42:16.150 --> 01:42:19.429
which they did until it felt even hotter to
the taste.

01:42:19.429 --> 01:42:23.560
One of the D Class’s fillings even fell
out, and eventually, the structural integrity

01:42:23.560 --> 01:42:30.039
of Subject A’s dive suit failed, presumably
disintegrated by the water from SCP-242.

01:42:30.039 --> 01:42:35.260
After a few muffled screams and gurgling noises,
Test Subject A wasn’t heard from again,

01:42:35.260 --> 01:42:38.079
and we can all probably guess why.

01:42:38.079 --> 01:42:42.920
As for Subject B, they kept drinking from
the barrel, suffering no adverse effects,

01:42:42.920 --> 01:42:45.670
even after seventeen long hours.

01:42:45.670 --> 01:42:50.380
There were no noticeable psychological or
physical changes, even their urine showed

01:42:50.380 --> 01:42:52.600
no traces of abnormality.

01:42:52.600 --> 01:42:58.079
The water from SCP-242 left in the barrel
evaporated as normal, leaving behind no residue

01:42:58.079 --> 01:43:03.789
or any indicator as to why taking the water
out of the pool made it safer to drink than

01:43:03.789 --> 01:43:06.310
the same water in the pool.

01:43:06.310 --> 01:43:10.979
Perhaps the moral of the story is to just
be careful where you choose to take a swim,

01:43:10.979 --> 01:43:14.920
otherwise, it could be your last.

01:43:14.920 --> 01:43:21.119
It was an ordinary night at Site 19 and Dr.
Smith was hard at work in his office.

01:43:21.119 --> 01:43:26.190
The overhead light was just about ready to
give out, the bulb dim and flickering, but

01:43:26.190 --> 01:43:30.229
there was no one available to change it at
the moment so he would just make do.

01:43:30.229 --> 01:43:33.760
Besides, he only had a little bit of work
left to finish.

01:43:33.760 --> 01:43:38.480
Hunched over his desk, eyes bleary and head
aching from too many hours of staring at a

01:43:38.480 --> 01:43:42.719
screen, he was ready to wrap up this report
and finally get home for some well-deserved

01:43:42.719 --> 01:43:43.719
rest.

01:43:43.719 --> 01:43:47.710
The constant anxiety of working with some
of the scariest monsters in the world was

01:43:47.710 --> 01:43:52.739
one thing, but the hours spent writing paperwork
on the monsters was an altogether different

01:43:52.739 --> 01:43:54.760
kind of terrifying.

01:43:54.760 --> 01:43:59.119
Most of the research staff had left for the
night, and only Dr. Smith and the usual security

01:43:59.119 --> 01:44:01.039
team remained in the building.

01:44:01.039 --> 01:44:06.640
There was no sound except the click of his
fingers on the keys, his occasional exhausted

01:44:06.640 --> 01:44:11.739
sigh, and the infrequent sound of footsteps
in the hall outside as a security officer

01:44:11.739 --> 01:44:13.260
made his rounds.

01:44:13.260 --> 01:44:18.179
Dr. Smith leaned back in his chair, stretching
his arms over his head and feeling his back

01:44:18.179 --> 01:44:19.570
crack.

01:44:19.570 --> 01:44:20.570
Almost done.

01:44:20.570 --> 01:44:25.099
He recalled, dimly, a thermos of tea he had
left on the shelf behind him.

01:44:25.099 --> 01:44:29.150
Perhaps that would be the kick he needed to
finish this work up and get home to his bath,

01:44:29.150 --> 01:44:31.459
his books, and his pet cat Roger.

01:44:31.459 --> 01:44:35.860
He swiveled his chair around, preparing to
stand up and retrieve the thermos when he

01:44:35.860 --> 01:44:39.110
suddenly came face to face with a nightmare.

01:44:39.110 --> 01:44:46.249
There, less than an inch from him, was a smooth
featureless face, black as the night and devoid

01:44:46.249 --> 01:44:47.519
of any expression.

01:44:47.519 --> 01:44:54.420
It was hunched over, its face peering into
him, despite not having any eyes itself.

01:44:54.420 --> 01:44:59.610
Without a sound, without so much as a creak
of the door, this thing had come into his

01:44:59.610 --> 01:45:04.110
office and appeared behind him, waiting for
him to turn around and see it.

01:45:04.110 --> 01:45:08.880
Dr. Smith let out a shriek of terror, knocking
his chair over as he scrambled to get away

01:45:08.880 --> 01:45:09.880
from the intruder.

01:45:09.880 --> 01:45:14.659
His heart pounding in his ears, he tore past
the dark figure, yanking open the door to

01:45:14.659 --> 01:45:18.039
his office and taking off running down the
hall.

01:45:18.039 --> 01:45:22.459
He called out for help, for someone, anyone,
to come.

01:45:22.459 --> 01:45:26.369
Several security personnel heard his cries
and rushed to see what had happened.

01:45:26.369 --> 01:45:30.959
They found a shivering Dr. Smith, babbling
about a “demon” in his office and repeating

01:45:30.959 --> 01:45:34.709
“it doesn’t have a face” over and over
again.

01:45:34.709 --> 01:45:39.479
Once he had calmed down - and finally been
given that cup of tea - Dr. Smith was informed

01:45:39.479 --> 01:45:44.729
that as stressful as that encounter might
have been, he was never really in any danger.

01:45:44.729 --> 01:45:49.559
We don’t have another SCP-173 on our hands
here, thankfully.

01:45:49.559 --> 01:45:52.499
This statue isn’t murderous or even violent.

01:45:52.499 --> 01:45:57.439
To the best of our observational ability,
we’ve determined that this particular surprisingly

01:45:57.439 --> 01:46:01.170
mobile statue is just kind of a jerk.

01:46:01.170 --> 01:46:07.749
SCP-650, nicknamed “The Startling Statue,”
is a stylized black statue of a humanoid figure,

01:46:07.749 --> 01:46:10.749
standing at 167 centimeters tall.

01:46:10.749 --> 01:46:16.250
It has no hands or facial features, its arms
ending in rounded points, and its face and

01:46:16.250 --> 01:46:19.459
head a smooth surface like that of a mannequin.

01:46:19.459 --> 01:46:24.520
When the statue is dormant, or at least resting
and waiting for its next chance to move, it

01:46:24.520 --> 01:46:29.560
stands straight and reaches upwards, head
tilted up as if its nonexistent eyes are watching

01:46:29.560 --> 01:46:31.110
the sky.

01:46:31.110 --> 01:46:35.770
Attempts to determine the materials the statue
is made of have proved inconclusive.

01:46:35.770 --> 01:46:40.110
Some tests show an impossibly large combination
of different materials, where other tests

01:46:40.110 --> 01:46:44.219
came back with no matches for any recognized
materials at all.

01:46:44.219 --> 01:46:48.900
If no one is observing the statue, it will
move to a place immediately behind whoever

01:46:48.900 --> 01:46:53.229
is in the room with it, switching its pose
to a more threatening one.

01:46:53.229 --> 01:46:58.999
It moves silently, and no one has been able
to capture evidence of its method of locomotion.

01:46:58.999 --> 01:47:04.079
All that is known is that it does in fact
move, and it always appears extremely close

01:47:04.079 --> 01:47:09.170
to the subject of its interest, in order to
provoke a strong fight-or-flight reaction.

01:47:09.170 --> 01:47:14.459
The statue seems to have no interest in harming
those it frightens, never touching or directly

01:47:14.459 --> 01:47:16.289
interacting with anyone.

01:47:16.289 --> 01:47:22.100
It only seems interested in startling its
victims, if you can even call them “victims.”

01:47:22.100 --> 01:47:27.210
It can be unpleasant to be unexpectedly frightened
like that, sure, but you get the same experience

01:47:27.210 --> 01:47:32.670
at most Halloween attractions or horror movies,
and people pay good money for those.

01:47:32.670 --> 01:47:37.059
Several trials were conducted in order to
determine the statue’s pattern of behavior.

01:47:37.059 --> 01:47:41.480
In each trial, an SCP Foundation agent was
assigned to stand in the statue’s containment

01:47:41.480 --> 01:47:44.479
unit and watch the object for a period of
time.

01:47:44.479 --> 01:47:49.020
When prompted by a researcher in another room,
speaking to them via radio, they were ordered

01:47:49.020 --> 01:47:51.110
to look away from the statue.

01:47:51.110 --> 01:47:54.170
Once cleared to look at the statue again,
they were ordered to look around the room

01:47:54.170 --> 01:47:57.420
and report where it went, and what it was
doing.

01:47:57.420 --> 01:48:02.309
In most of the experiments, the statue appeared
directly behind the personnel, angled with

01:48:02.309 --> 01:48:07.439
its arms reaching toward them and its head
glaring down at them, as if about to attack.

01:48:07.439 --> 01:48:12.350
In nearly every trial, the statue hit the
same position, and the Agent looking at it

01:48:12.350 --> 01:48:14.489
was startled to the point of screaming.

01:48:14.489 --> 01:48:17.820
There was even talk of cutting footage of
all of the screams together into a video that

01:48:17.820 --> 01:48:20.239
would be shown at the company Christmas party.

01:48:20.239 --> 01:48:25.170
However, in three cases, the statue adopted
a different pose as well as position in the

01:48:25.170 --> 01:48:30.599
room, much to the surprise and confusion of
the team conducting the experiments.

01:48:30.599 --> 01:48:34.709
When Agent Dunne was assigned to observe the
statue, he was asked to close his eyes for

01:48:34.709 --> 01:48:38.829
five seconds and wait for SCP-650 to move.

01:48:38.829 --> 01:48:42.969
When he opened his eyes, the first thing he
did was whirl around and look behind him,

01:48:42.969 --> 01:48:45.400
having heard about the results of the previous
tests.

01:48:45.400 --> 01:48:49.860
However, when he turned to face the statue,
there was nothing there.

01:48:49.860 --> 01:48:53.840
He turned back around to his original stance,
preparing to radio Command and tell them the

01:48:53.840 --> 01:48:57.550
statue was gone, when he let out a yelp of
surprise.

01:48:57.550 --> 01:49:01.789
There, at the table in the corner several
feet away, was the statue.

01:49:01.789 --> 01:49:06.729
It was lying on the table with its arms behind
its head, as if relaxing, with the area considered

01:49:06.729 --> 01:49:09.730
to be its “face” turned directly toward
Dunne.

01:49:09.730 --> 01:49:13.409
Unsettled by the surprise, and definitely
uncomfortable with how the statue seemed to

01:49:13.409 --> 01:49:17.270
be looking at him, he left the room without
another word.

01:49:17.270 --> 01:49:21.689
At another point in the trials, Agent Riley
pulled the short straw and was told to enter

01:49:21.689 --> 01:49:23.280
650’s containment.

01:49:23.280 --> 01:49:27.389
She stood in the center of the room and stared
at the statue in front of her for a long period

01:49:27.389 --> 01:49:28.459
of time.

01:49:28.459 --> 01:49:32.909
When given the command, she closed her eyes
and waited for a duration of 30 seconds.

01:49:32.909 --> 01:49:37.289
Much like Agent Dunne, her first instinct
on opening her eyes was to turn around and

01:49:37.289 --> 01:49:40.590
look behind her, ready to see the statue there.

01:49:40.590 --> 01:49:44.729
Instead, however, it was sitting on a chair
at the other end of the room, the points where

01:49:44.729 --> 01:49:47.760
its hands should be neatly folded in its lap.

01:49:47.760 --> 01:49:51.710
Its body was facing away from Agent Riley,
but even though she was looking at what could

01:49:51.710 --> 01:49:56.079
have easily been the back of the statue’s
head, she later reported the distinct sense

01:49:56.079 --> 01:49:57.840
that it was looking at her.

01:49:57.840 --> 01:50:02.500
Though she didn’t scream like her colleagues
had when it was their turn to watch the statue,

01:50:02.500 --> 01:50:07.360
she confessed to feeling an overwhelming sense
of unease, and her hands would not stop shaking

01:50:07.360 --> 01:50:09.749
for the next several hours.

01:50:09.749 --> 01:50:14.499
These two instances of the statue adopting
a casual posture and keeping its distance

01:50:14.499 --> 01:50:19.590
from its observers were bizarre, but the final
break from the statue’s usual behavior was

01:50:19.590 --> 01:50:21.789
the strangest of them all.

01:50:21.789 --> 01:50:26.800
Agent Cho was sent into SCP-650’s containment
and told to stand with his back against the

01:50:26.800 --> 01:50:28.280
wall of his choice.

01:50:28.280 --> 01:50:33.030
The plan was to determine what the statue
would do if its usual favorite position, just

01:50:33.030 --> 01:50:36.360
behind the observer, was no longer an option.

01:50:36.360 --> 01:50:41.599
If there was no space behind Agent Cho, then
the statue could not turn up there.

01:50:41.599 --> 01:50:46.079
Once he was settled into his spot and had
been watching the statue for several minutes,

01:50:46.079 --> 01:50:49.139
Agent Cho closed his eyes for exactly one
minute.

01:50:49.139 --> 01:50:53.320
When he opened them, he immediately scanned
the room to see where the statue had gone.

01:50:53.320 --> 01:50:58.409
It was not at the table or the chair, nor
was it standing in its original place in front

01:50:58.409 --> 01:50:59.409
of him.

01:50:59.409 --> 01:51:01.159
Finally, he spotted it.

01:51:01.159 --> 01:51:06.019
The statue was huddled in the corner of the
room, curled up in an approximation of the

01:51:06.019 --> 01:51:07.300
fetal position.

01:51:07.300 --> 01:51:12.190
Its head was down, and its arms were held
up in front of its face as if trying to protect

01:51:12.190 --> 01:51:13.190
itself.

01:51:13.190 --> 01:51:17.729
Though he could not explain why, Agent Cho
got a distinct impression that the statue

01:51:17.729 --> 01:51:18.969
was afraid.

01:51:18.969 --> 01:51:23.169
His stomach dropped at the sight, and he would
later admit to his supervisor that he briefly

01:51:23.169 --> 01:51:27.030
thought about trying to comfort SCP-650 somehow.

01:51:27.030 --> 01:51:32.320
The impulse passed, but Cho was left with
a mixture of anxiety and guilt as if he had

01:51:32.320 --> 01:51:34.889
done something wrong and upset the statue.

01:51:34.889 --> 01:51:38.619
The sensation did not pass until he was out
of the room.

01:51:38.619 --> 01:51:44.659
It is not entirely clear why the statue chose
these alternative poses during these particular

01:51:44.659 --> 01:51:45.659
experiments.

01:51:45.659 --> 01:51:49.199
The prevailing theory among the research team
is that these are simply other tools in its

01:51:49.199 --> 01:51:54.059
arsenal, methods that it can use to elicit
a strong reaction from a person who is less

01:51:54.059 --> 01:51:57.320
likely to be startled by its usual trick.

01:51:57.320 --> 01:52:03.790
Following the incident with Dr. Smith, SCP-650
was upgraded from Safe Class to Euclid Class.

01:52:03.790 --> 01:52:08.439
Just to clarify, for the people in the back:
Euclid Class SCP’s are not necessarily considered

01:52:08.439 --> 01:52:14.209
to be dangerous but require more effort to
contain than objects classified as Safe.

01:52:14.209 --> 01:52:19.610
Most SCP’s that display autonomy or independent
thought, but are not overtly hostile toward

01:52:19.610 --> 01:52:22.330
humanity, are classified as Euclid.

01:52:22.330 --> 01:52:26.349
Along with its updated status, special containment
procedures have been employed in order to

01:52:26.349 --> 01:52:30.829
keep this Startling Statue from making any
more surprise escapes.

01:52:30.829 --> 01:52:35.939
SCP-650 is to be stored in a locked room,
4 meters by 4 meters.

01:52:35.939 --> 01:52:41.280
It is to be kept under constant surveillance
by at least three personnel at any given time,

01:52:41.280 --> 01:52:45.449
standing so that the SCP and at least one
of the observers are visible to them at all

01:52:45.449 --> 01:52:46.679
times.

01:52:46.679 --> 01:52:51.320
They are allowed to watch the statue remotely,
via security camera, as long as they remain

01:52:51.320 --> 01:52:53.380
focused on the SCP.

01:52:53.380 --> 01:52:55.350
This method is only to be employed in case
of emergency.

01:52:55.350 --> 01:53:00.689
A great deal of the Foundation budget was
dedicated to maintaining up-to-date containment

01:53:00.689 --> 01:53:05.389
facilities for SCP-650, as demanded in a note
from Dr. Smith.

01:53:05.389 --> 01:53:06.760
in the official file for SCP-650.

01:53:06.760 --> 01:53:12.210
The note reads: “I don't give a flying rat
about the budget; keep this damn thing contained!

01:53:12.210 --> 01:53:16.469
Turning around in a dim office to see this
thing a half-inch away from your nose is guaranteed

01:53:16.469 --> 01:53:17.969
to take years from your life.

01:53:17.969 --> 01:53:21.820
And given what we deal with, we don't have
many to spare.”

01:53:21.820 --> 01:53:25.030
So, what does the Startling Statue want?

01:53:25.030 --> 01:53:29.999
Why does it use its power of mobility to scare
people but never do anything beyond that?

01:53:29.999 --> 01:53:33.969
No one is certain, and the Foundation has
too many other fires to put out to bother

01:53:33.969 --> 01:53:37.119
looking further into a clearly benign entity.

01:53:37.119 --> 01:53:42.119
Unfortunately, there are questions about SCP-650
that will never be answered, and there is

01:53:42.119 --> 01:53:44.689
so much about it we will never know.

01:53:44.689 --> 01:53:46.400
One thing is for sure, though.

01:53:46.400 --> 01:53:50.750
If you find yourself alone in a room with
an unsettling statue, you had better keep

01:53:50.750 --> 01:53:52.119
an eye on it.

01:53:52.119 --> 01:53:54.460
Just in case.

01:53:54.460 --> 01:53:56.709
BOO!

01:53:56.709 --> 01:53:59.310
Well hello there, boils and ghouls!

01:53:59.310 --> 01:54:05.169
We hope we didn’t startle you too hard there,
it’s only us, your good old friends at SCP

01:54:05.169 --> 01:54:06.300
Explained.

01:54:06.300 --> 01:54:09.300
We all love a little fright now and then,
don’t we?

01:54:09.300 --> 01:54:15.229
After all, that would explain our fascination
with the morbid tales of the SCP Foundation.

01:54:15.229 --> 01:54:21.050
Rotten old men who can walk through walls,
and tear you limb from limb in their own private

01:54:21.050 --> 01:54:22.460
hells?

01:54:22.460 --> 01:54:27.709
Nightmarish Sarkic diseases that turn anyone
who touches them into a horrible abomination?

01:54:27.709 --> 01:54:31.900
Evil masks that kill you and take over your
body, using it to do acts of great cruelty

01:54:31.900 --> 01:54:34.409
until you melt down into black goo?

01:54:34.409 --> 01:54:37.559
Oh...You’re not scared of those?

01:54:37.559 --> 01:54:42.650
You think you’re so tough, so prepared for
anything, that even those anomalous beings

01:54:42.650 --> 01:54:47.270
of pure terror can’t break through the impenetrable
shell of your bravery?

01:54:47.270 --> 01:54:51.840
Well...I suppose we better bring out the big
guns, then.

01:54:51.840 --> 01:54:57.099
Just remember, when you’re huddled in the
corner, bones rattling in fear, that you brought

01:54:57.099 --> 01:54:59.579
this on yourself.

01:54:59.579 --> 01:55:07.760
After all, there’s no entity quite as good
at inspiring screams as SCP-2006.

01:55:07.760 --> 01:55:13.380
So please stay awhile, and find out why this
one’s called...Too Spooky.

01:55:13.380 --> 01:55:15.860
We’re sorry you had to hear that.

01:55:15.860 --> 01:55:20.409
But you really can’t blame us for having
a little theatricality with this one - In

01:55:20.409 --> 01:55:24.550
fact, having a good grasp of theatricality
is actually essential to everyone dealing

01:55:24.550 --> 01:55:25.550
with SCP-2006.

01:55:25.550 --> 01:55:33.579
Forget gunplay, rituals, and mind games, SCP-2006
requires Foundation-subsidised acting lessons

01:55:33.579 --> 01:55:35.709
in order to work on his containment.

01:55:35.709 --> 01:55:40.800
Which, even as Foundation containment methods
go, is pretty darn strange.

01:55:40.800 --> 01:55:44.840
When you got into this line of work, you probably
expected you’d be in high-intensity battles

01:55:44.840 --> 01:55:50.060
with SCP-682, or attending conferences on
how best to repel the menace of The Scarlet

01:55:50.060 --> 01:55:55.780
King - Not acting out scenes from A Streetcar
Named Desire with Dr. Bright.

01:55:55.780 --> 01:55:58.239
But believe us, it’s important work.

01:55:58.239 --> 01:56:03.769
As they’ll probably tell you at these classes,
“There are no small parts, only small actors.”

01:56:03.769 --> 01:56:08.639
You won’t spend time at these sessions perfecting
Shakespearian soliloquies, instead, you’ll

01:56:08.639 --> 01:56:14.510
be adopting a much narrower focus: Learning
how to properly act and express fear.

01:56:14.510 --> 01:56:17.739
The more convincingly scared you can appear,
the better.

01:56:17.739 --> 01:56:23.510
Because when it comes to SCP-2006, your job
and potentially even your life depend on it.

01:56:23.510 --> 01:56:27.489
Plus, it’s the only time that peeing your
pants and collapsing on the job may actually

01:56:27.489 --> 01:56:32.579
get you a raise, rather than just a series
of strange looks from your co-workers.

01:56:32.579 --> 01:56:37.019
When you pass that course with flying colors,
you’re finally ready to actually come face

01:56:37.019 --> 01:56:42.199
to face with the Prince of Nightmares himself:
SCP-2006.

01:56:42.199 --> 01:56:46.110
By this point, you’ve had it drilled into
your head so many times that you could never

01:56:46.110 --> 01:56:51.429
forget it: For the love of God, whatever this
thing does, you act scared.

01:56:51.429 --> 01:56:56.590
Don’t stonewall, don’t smile, and whatever
you do, don’t laugh.

01:56:56.590 --> 01:57:01.360
Laughing at SCP-2006 is probably the fastest
way you can get demoted to swabbing feces

01:57:01.360 --> 01:57:04.219
in SCP-173’s chamber.

01:57:04.219 --> 01:57:07.699
If you know what’s good for you, you’ll
dial up that fear.

01:57:07.699 --> 01:57:12.249
When the big day comes, you’re sent into
SCP-2006’s airtight containment chamber

01:57:12.249 --> 01:57:14.199
with a special package.

01:57:14.199 --> 01:57:19.150
That time of the month has come once again
- You need to deliver the goods.

01:57:19.150 --> 01:57:23.559
You spot a television in the corner first,
still on but tuned to static.

01:57:23.559 --> 01:57:28.619
You’re pondering what a waste of electricity
this is when SCP-2006, who’d been hiding

01:57:28.619 --> 01:57:32.400
behind an armchair, decided to finally strike.

01:57:32.400 --> 01:57:36.800
You barely had time to realize what was going
on when a large, dark shape suddenly blotted

01:57:36.800 --> 01:57:38.050
out your vision.

01:57:38.050 --> 01:57:43.349
It was over six feet tall, and it looked...Well,
it looked like a man in an exceedingly cheap

01:57:43.349 --> 01:57:49.699
gorilla costume, except with a goofy diving
helmet with what looked like TV antennas on

01:57:49.699 --> 01:57:50.699
top.

01:57:50.699 --> 01:57:54.599
It waved its arms around wildly, as if to
hammer home the point that, yes, this really

01:57:54.599 --> 01:57:58.119
was happening, and you should be terrified
by it.

01:57:58.119 --> 01:58:01.090
The creature bellowed, “FEAR ME MORTAL.

01:58:01.090 --> 01:58:04.119
I AM THE MIGHTY RO-MAN!

01:58:04.119 --> 01:58:05.939
COWER IN FEAAAAAAAR!”

01:58:05.939 --> 01:58:10.679
At that moment, your weeks of training kicked
in, almost like a reflex.

01:58:10.679 --> 01:58:15.500
You let out an ear-piercing shriek and drop
down to the floor, desperately crawling away

01:58:15.500 --> 01:58:17.249
from the goofy-looking creature.

01:58:17.249 --> 01:58:21.420
Eyes wide, breathing heavy, movements frantic
and defensive.

01:58:21.420 --> 01:58:25.249
You gather yourself up in one of the room’s
corners and curl into a ball, covering your

01:58:25.249 --> 01:58:26.249
face.

01:58:26.249 --> 01:58:29.260
Imbuing your voice with a well-practiced quiver,
you say, “Please mighty Ro-Man!

01:58:29.260 --> 01:58:30.260
Don't h-hurt me!

01:58:30.260 --> 01:58:33.519
I have so much to live for, just please, let
me go!”

01:58:33.519 --> 01:58:39.110
The monster holds a, quote-unquote, “menacing”
pose for a few seconds longer, before slackening

01:58:39.110 --> 01:58:40.679
into a joyful laugh.

01:58:40.679 --> 01:58:44.400
It even extended a rubbery gorilla paw to
help you up.

01:58:44.400 --> 01:58:48.429
Of course, you hesitate for a few seconds,
gazing fearfully, waiting for it to say.

01:58:48.429 --> 01:58:49.429
“Ha ha ha!

01:58:49.429 --> 01:58:50.429
It's just me, doc!

01:58:50.429 --> 01:58:52.280
I got you pretty good, didn't I?”

01:58:52.280 --> 01:58:55.119
And as far as he knows, yes, he did.

01:58:55.119 --> 01:58:58.260
You’re sure to never slip into the body
language of comfort.

01:58:58.260 --> 01:59:04.460
It’s utterly vital that SCP-2006 truly believes
that he’s scary to you, even though he looks

01:59:04.460 --> 01:59:08.140
like a terrible monster costume from an even
worse low-budget B-Movie.

01:59:08.140 --> 01:59:14.769
Though specifically, the Ro-Man, the monster
from the 1953 trash classic, “Robot Monster.”

01:59:14.769 --> 01:59:20.600
You tell SCP-2006 that you’re here with
some more stimulus material for him, and hand

01:59:20.600 --> 01:59:22.380
him a plastic bag.

01:59:22.380 --> 01:59:25.789
When he asks you what you’ve brought him
this time, you tell him you can’t even look

01:59:25.789 --> 01:59:26.789
at it.

01:59:26.789 --> 01:59:31.270
If you so much as laid eyes on it, you’d
slip into a terrified state of catatonia.

01:59:31.270 --> 01:59:36.099
You’d honestly rather look at 096 than look
at what you’ve brought him today.

01:59:36.099 --> 01:59:41.500
SCP-2006 cocked his head to the side, and
asked, “What’s 096?”

01:59:41.500 --> 01:59:42.749
Oh no.

01:59:42.749 --> 01:59:45.610
The terror that was fake before wasn’t quite
so fake now.

01:59:45.610 --> 01:59:50.400
You’d slipped up, buddy, and if you didn’t
come up with a good save quickly, you would

01:59:50.400 --> 01:59:51.479
be in deep trouble.

01:59:51.479 --> 01:59:55.700
You gulp and take a quick breath, trying to
compose yourself, before saying that 096 is

01:59:55.700 --> 01:59:57.229
just another movie.

01:59:57.229 --> 02:00:00.269
One that’s not nearly as scary as the one
you’ve prepared for him.

02:00:00.269 --> 02:00:05.269
That seemed to satisfy him, so you internally
breathe a sigh of relief, and turn to make

02:00:05.269 --> 02:00:06.269
your exit.

02:00:06.269 --> 02:00:12.889
You’ve just left SCP-2006 with a DVD copy
of the 1977 “classic”, Death Bed: The

02:00:12.889 --> 02:00:14.199
Bed That Eats.

02:00:14.199 --> 02:00:17.960
A somewhat obscure horror movie about an evil
bed created by a demon.

02:00:17.960 --> 02:00:20.929
That should tide the eccentric anomaly over
for another month.

02:00:20.929 --> 02:00:24.829
So, you’re probably wondering: What actually
just happened?

02:00:24.829 --> 02:00:26.130
What’s the logic?

02:00:26.130 --> 02:00:30.550
What are the connections between the strange
sequence of events we all just witnessed?

02:00:30.550 --> 02:00:36.610
While it may seem bizarre now, once you know
more about SCP-2006, it’ll all make sense.

02:00:36.610 --> 02:00:41.150
We can’t promise it’ll actually seem any
less bizarre by the end, though.

02:00:41.150 --> 02:00:44.429
SCP-2006 is a Keter-class shapeshifting anomaly.

02:00:44.429 --> 02:00:48.849
Its default form is a floating sphere of about
fifty centimeters in diameter.

02:00:48.849 --> 02:00:55.499
Not exactly terrifying - And this is actually
a big problem for SCP-2006, as the mischievous

02:00:55.499 --> 02:00:59.219
anomaly has an almost compulsive desire to
scare people.

02:00:59.219 --> 02:01:04.229
Not to physically harm them in any way, just
give them a good, old-fashioned spook.

02:01:04.229 --> 02:01:09.110
He’s shown to be pretty much indestructible,
so neutralization is off the table.

02:01:09.110 --> 02:01:12.630
You may be thinking, “He seems like a pretty
harmless goofball, why would anyone want to

02:01:12.630 --> 02:01:14.119
neutralize him?”

02:01:14.119 --> 02:01:17.559
And...Well, we’ll answer that one later.

02:01:17.559 --> 02:01:21.599
Back to SCP-2006’s favorite hobby: Scaring
people.

02:01:21.599 --> 02:01:25.909
While 2006 seems to practically live off of
giving a good scare, he’s thankfully no

02:01:25.909 --> 02:01:26.919
Pennywise.

02:01:26.919 --> 02:01:32.190
2006 has no inherent knowledge of what scares
humans, and thus, has to learn what scares

02:01:32.190 --> 02:01:34.709
humans from external sources.

02:01:34.709 --> 02:01:40.769
This unique weakness to SCP-2006’s ability
is one the Foundation has discovered an ingenious

02:01:40.769 --> 02:01:46.869
method of exploiting for its containment:
They simply keep SCP-2006 misinformed on what

02:01:46.869 --> 02:01:52.429
people actually find scary, tricking it to
make sure that it’s always hopelessly inept

02:01:52.429 --> 02:01:53.429
at its hobby.

02:01:53.429 --> 02:01:55.480
Their method of achieving this is twofold.

02:01:55.480 --> 02:02:01.689
Firstly, they give SCP-2006 a monthly supply
of the worst horror movies you can imagine.

02:02:01.689 --> 02:02:07.860
True bargain bucket B-movie schlock: Troll
2, Leprechaun: In The Hood, Birdemic: Shock

02:02:07.860 --> 02:02:14.189
&amp; Terror, The Gingerdead Man, The Beast of
Yucca Flats, Plan 9 From Outer Space, The

02:02:14.189 --> 02:02:19.559
Creeping Terror, The Man Without a Body, Manos:
The Hands of Fate, Track of the Moon Beast,

02:02:19.559 --> 02:02:25.820
and of course, the seminal classic, Eegah
- A movie about an evil caveman being unfrozen

02:02:25.820 --> 02:02:29.769
and terrorizing Palm Springs.

02:02:29.769 --> 02:02:35.749
Movies like this are a perfect mechanism for
tricking SCP-2006, because it sees the characters

02:02:35.749 --> 02:02:41.100
in the movies reacting with fear to the terrible,
hokey monsters rampaging across backlots and

02:02:41.100 --> 02:02:46.229
soundstages, and starts to believe that these
B-Movie beasts are actually scary.

02:02:46.229 --> 02:02:49.269
That’s the first part of the trick, and
you’ve probably already figured out the

02:02:49.269 --> 02:02:54.619
second half: The Foundation makes sure that
any employees who interact with SCP-2006 in

02:02:54.619 --> 02:03:00.499
any capacity must play the part of appearing
actually, genuinely frightened by it.

02:03:00.499 --> 02:03:05.150
This one-two punch of trickery keeps SCP-2006
successfully bamboozled.

02:03:05.150 --> 02:03:09.380
As such, despite being a creature largely
based around creating fear - albeit, in a

02:03:09.380 --> 02:03:14.579
more friendly, playful way than most anomalies
- it’s seen as a joke among staff members.

02:03:14.579 --> 02:03:19.630
It wouldn’t be surprising to hear that different
staff members took turns laughing at surveillance

02:03:19.630 --> 02:03:20.630
footage.

02:03:20.630 --> 02:03:25.690
Or that at the latest Site Halloween Party,
a few drunken researchers tried to trick SCP-2006

02:03:25.690 --> 02:03:32.999
into assuming the form of David S. Pumpkins
from Saturday Night Live.

02:03:32.999 --> 02:03:39.269
As you could probably gather, developing such
an unimpressed attitude to containing anomalies

02:03:39.269 --> 02:03:42.560
with the SCP Foundation is never a good thing.

02:03:42.560 --> 02:03:47.499
After all, even some of the most innocent-looking
ones can hide surprisingly dark secrets.

02:03:47.499 --> 02:03:52.940
Dr. Randall Owings, the Site Director for
Site 118 - where SCP-2006 is held - released

02:03:52.940 --> 02:03:55.979
a stern memorandum to everyone working in
2006’s proximity.

02:03:55.979 --> 02:03:56.979
It read:

02:03:56.979 --> 02:04:03.059
“I have been getting reports of some of
the lax behavior regarding SCP-2006.

02:04:03.059 --> 02:04:08.099
Many personnel have been heard laughing at
SCP-2006 during surveillance when it watches

02:04:08.099 --> 02:04:11.499
a new movie, or when it attempts to scare
individuals.

02:04:11.499 --> 02:04:16.820
Some personnel have been heard questioning
why SCP-2006 is classified as a Keter entity.

02:04:16.820 --> 02:04:22.940
I am here to remind you that a Keter entity
is a Keter entity, regardless of how innocuous

02:04:22.940 --> 02:04:24.289
it may seem.

02:04:24.289 --> 02:04:30.480
No, SCP-2006 is not a rampaging demi-god,
nor is it a regenerating super lizard.

02:04:30.480 --> 02:04:35.860
However, it possesses the same level of danger
as any other Keter that the Foundation has

02:04:35.860 --> 02:04:36.860
contained.

02:04:36.860 --> 02:04:38.239
Think of SCP-2006's purpose.

02:04:38.239 --> 02:04:40.219
It wishes to scare people.

02:04:40.219 --> 02:04:45.860
Imagine what would happen if SCP-2006 broke
containment, and found out what really scared

02:04:45.860 --> 02:04:46.860
people.

02:04:46.860 --> 02:04:52.090
Imagine if it saw the horror and fear of war,
or the concepts of paranoia or phobias common

02:04:52.090 --> 02:04:54.099
to each and every human being.

02:04:54.099 --> 02:04:59.919
Imagine if it found the true horror of a nuclear
holocaust or an XK-Class scenario.

02:04:59.919 --> 02:05:04.189
Now couple that with an entity that possesses
shape-shifting abilities with no known limits,

02:05:04.189 --> 02:05:07.309
and you'll understand why it's classified
as Keter.

02:05:07.309 --> 02:05:10.189
All personnel mentioned above have been suitably
disciplined.

02:05:10.189 --> 02:05:12.479
I do not want to hear about this again.”

02:05:12.479 --> 02:05:18.739
SCP-2006 is only as harmless as the Foundation’s
containment procedures allow it to be.

02:05:18.739 --> 02:05:23.849
It’s why it can never know about other anomalies
or any actually frightening works of fiction.

02:05:23.849 --> 02:05:30.270
If ever SCP-2006 became aware of the true
sources of human fear, there would be no stopping

02:05:30.270 --> 02:05:32.959
it, seeing as the creature appears to be indestructible.

02:05:32.959 --> 02:05:37.949
Like many of the anomalies kept under lock
and key by the SCP Foundation, it’s a ticking

02:05:37.949 --> 02:05:42.780
time bomb that one little mistake could turn
into an utter catastrophe.

02:05:42.780 --> 02:05:47.689
Terrible movies and theatrical staff members
need to keep SCP-2006 in the dark about what

02:05:47.689 --> 02:05:53.689
actually scares us, because, beyond that,
the only limit to the danger of SCP-2006 is

02:05:53.689 --> 02:05:55.610
the human imagination.

02:05:55.610 --> 02:05:59.579
And that, my friends, is a very spooky thought
indeed.

02:05:59.579 --> 02:06:05.619
An SCP Foundation researcher sits at a table
inside of a standard containment cell.

02:06:05.619 --> 02:06:10.719
These are often dangerous places to be, especially
when the SCP you’re supposed to be studying

02:06:10.719 --> 02:06:12.760
is one that you can’t see.

02:06:12.760 --> 02:06:18.309
The researcher is taking notes, unsure of
exactly what’s going to happen next.

02:06:18.309 --> 02:06:23.519
He can hear the sounds of knives scraping
behind, of flesh sizzling and searing from

02:06:23.519 --> 02:06:24.949
high heat.

02:06:24.949 --> 02:06:29.659
He braces himself as a burst of heat hits
the back of his head, as if a fireball has

02:06:29.659 --> 02:06:30.659
erupted.

02:06:30.659 --> 02:06:33.659
Just then it happens - an object floats through
the air and settles in front of him on the

02:06:33.659 --> 02:06:34.659
table.

02:06:34.659 --> 02:06:37.639
It’s a plate of food, and it looks delicious.

02:06:37.639 --> 02:06:42.670
It may surprise you to learn that there is
no rule that the SCP Foundation must deal

02:06:42.670 --> 02:06:46.329
exclusively with violent and vicious creatures.

02:06:46.329 --> 02:06:51.229
Not every SCP held in containment shares the
same malevolence and contempt for humanity

02:06:51.229 --> 02:06:58.940
as SCP-682, or the world-ending threat posed
by the likes of SCP-2317.

02:06:58.940 --> 02:07:05.060
Some - perhaps not many, but some - are benign
and might even seem outwardly friendly, but

02:07:05.060 --> 02:07:10.239
you’d still be taking a huge risk to assume
that anything contained by the SCP Foundation

02:07:10.239 --> 02:07:12.229
is completely harmless.

02:07:12.229 --> 02:07:15.669
Such is the case with SCP-5031.

02:07:15.669 --> 02:07:20.340
As per the Foundation’s containment procedures,
this quasi-humanoid – meaning it appears

02:07:20.340 --> 02:07:25.679
to have some vaguely human features - is held
in an airtight cell that is regularly checked

02:07:25.679 --> 02:07:29.400
by Foundation personnel on a bi-weekly basis.

02:07:29.400 --> 02:07:35.239
SCP-5031 has no need for regular nutrition
or regular interactions from staff.

02:07:35.239 --> 02:07:41.979
The trick with SCP-5031, is not being eaten
by it, since though it doesn’t need food,

02:07:41.979 --> 02:07:47.440
it does still hunt and consume anything it
encounters - human or otherwise.

02:07:47.440 --> 02:07:53.309
Avoiding being eaten is hard enough with creatures
that can actually be seen, but like so many

02:07:53.309 --> 02:07:59.630
other creatures the Foundation keeps contained,
SCP-5031 has developed an almost-perfect defense

02:07:59.630 --> 02:08:05.860
mechanism - which is that when observed, it
will literally cease to exist.

02:08:05.860 --> 02:08:10.199
Some might choose to refer to this as a ‘quantum
lock’, however it is worth noting that traces

02:08:10.199 --> 02:08:16.439
left by SCP-5031 still remain observable when
the creature has temporarily disappeared.

02:08:16.439 --> 02:08:22.530
For example, trails of blood and scratch marks
left behind by SCP-5031 still exist when the

02:08:22.530 --> 02:08:24.999
SCP itself does not.

02:08:24.999 --> 02:08:30.699
Naturally, this makes both avoiding the creature
and capturing it using cameras difficult.

02:08:30.699 --> 02:08:36.449
However, when SCP-5031’s existence ceases
it still casts a shadow.

02:08:36.449 --> 02:08:41.969
From this, researchers have been able to determine
several of the creature’s physical traits.

02:08:41.969 --> 02:08:47.059
Based on its silhouette, it has been deduced
that SCP-5031 levitates about half a meter

02:08:47.059 --> 02:08:52.229
above ground level, it sports an abnormally
small, neckless head atop an elongated torso

02:08:52.229 --> 02:08:59.429
- approximately 1.9 meters long - with three
sets of spindly lower arms that branch outwards.

02:08:59.429 --> 02:09:05.139
Using these arms and its loosely hanging body,
SCP-5031 will lower itself to hunt any human

02:09:05.139 --> 02:09:11.989
or animal that draws near to it and uses the
bladelike tail to cut up food.

02:09:11.989 --> 02:09:17.510
Perhaps the most interesting facet of SCP-5031
beyond its defensive capabilities and apparent

02:09:17.510 --> 02:09:23.399
physical attributes, are the series of nine
tests conducted by Senior Researcher Stanley

02:09:23.399 --> 02:09:24.659
Huxtable.

02:09:24.659 --> 02:09:28.419
Appalled by the conditions that the creature
was being kept in, Huxtable took over the

02:09:28.419 --> 02:09:32.570
role of HCL Supervisor for SCP-5031.

02:09:32.570 --> 02:09:37.130
Having grown increasingly frustrated and empathetic
towards the creature, listening to its screams

02:09:37.130 --> 02:09:43.400
from inside its iron containment unit, Huxtable
devised a series of tests to introduce SCP-5031

02:09:43.400 --> 02:09:48.280
to various different stimuli as a way to better
understand the creature and hopefully keep

02:09:48.280 --> 02:09:52.539
it contained in a way that didn’t seem to
cause so much suffering.

02:09:52.539 --> 02:09:57.679
It's worth remembering that the SCP Foundation
makes it its mission to be cold, not cruel,

02:09:57.679 --> 02:10:02.559
in performing their duties to protect normality
and many of the researchers and staff are

02:10:02.559 --> 02:10:08.579
just as capable of having empathy for creatures
as you might for a stray animal at a shelter.

02:10:08.579 --> 02:10:13.920
The first of Huxtable’s tests involved installing
speakers in SCP-5031’s cell, through which

02:10:13.920 --> 02:10:17.989
a variety of different ambient and popular
pieces of music were played to see if they

02:10:17.989 --> 02:10:21.099
had any effect on reducing the creature’s
stress.

02:10:21.099 --> 02:10:27.110
By judging SCP-5031’s stress levels based
on how much it screamed when compared to normal,

02:10:27.110 --> 02:10:31.739
Huxtable was able to determine how to best
to use music to calm the creature.

02:10:31.739 --> 02:10:36.630
SCP-5031 seemed to convey higher levels of
stress when listening to ‘Morning Forest’,

02:10:36.630 --> 02:10:41.869
‘Deep Grotto’ and ‘Seaside Paradise’
ambience, as well as the best of late 60s

02:10:41.869 --> 02:10:43.619
British rock band Jethro Tull.

02:10:43.619 --> 02:10:48.949
However, the best of Mozart, Enya, KISS and
Ben Folds produced dramatically different

02:10:48.949 --> 02:10:53.280
results, decreasing SCP-5031’s apparent
stress.

02:10:53.280 --> 02:10:57.789
Following this test, Senior Researcher Huxtable
compiled a playlist featuring SCP-5031’s

02:10:57.789 --> 02:10:59.650
favorite music.

02:10:59.650 --> 02:11:05.630
Over time, the stress-reducing effects of
music on SCP-5031 seemed to decrease, but

02:11:05.630 --> 02:11:09.399
keeping the playlist on shuffle seemed to
keep the creature consistently calmer than

02:11:09.399 --> 02:11:11.959
it had been previously.

02:11:11.959 --> 02:11:17.570
The next test involved introducing inanimate
objects into SCP-5031’s enclosure to monitor

02:11:17.570 --> 02:11:20.719
its reactions and how its stress levels were
affected.

02:11:20.719 --> 02:11:26.639
When a softball was thrown into the enclosure,
SCP-5031 immediately sliced the ball in two

02:11:26.639 --> 02:11:29.110
with its tail in one swift motion.

02:11:29.110 --> 02:11:33.329
A similar result occurred when researchers
threw the creature a basketball, which was

02:11:33.329 --> 02:11:36.880
quickly punctured and sliced open by SCP-5031’s
tail.

02:11:36.880 --> 02:11:42.159
Its stress levels first seemed to diminish
when the creature was offered a bowling ball,

02:11:42.159 --> 02:11:46.489
which it rolled around the enclosure and then
later knocked against a second bowling ball.

02:11:46.489 --> 02:11:53.059
However, when one of the balls chipped, rendering
it unable to roll properly, SCP-5031’s stress

02:11:53.059 --> 02:11:57.499
increased dramatically, until a replacement
was offered.

02:11:57.499 --> 02:12:02.230
Researcher Huxtable noted that SCP-5031 seemed
to possess a similar level of motor skills

02:12:02.230 --> 02:12:07.929
to an average human toddler, with similarly
explosive emotional reactions to match.

02:12:07.929 --> 02:12:13.460
Next, when given the choice between two food
sources at opposite ends of its enclosure,

02:12:13.460 --> 02:12:18.919
SCP-5031 seemed to gravitate towards higher-quality
food, most notably favoring cooked rotisserie

02:12:18.919 --> 02:12:21.070
chickens over animal carcasses.

02:12:21.070 --> 02:12:26.619
It even chose this option over a live chicken,
using its tail to cut its food into more manageable

02:12:26.619 --> 02:12:31.329
bite-sized portions, rather than ripping its
meat with its hands or teeth like many of

02:12:31.329 --> 02:12:34.280
its fellow SCPs.

02:12:34.280 --> 02:12:38.599
Researcher Huxtable recorded these findings
and highlighted that, even though SCP-5031

02:12:38.599 --> 02:12:43.969
didn’t need to eat in order to survive,
providing the creature with food of a better

02:12:43.969 --> 02:12:47.939
quality marginally reduced its stress.

02:12:47.939 --> 02:12:53.019
Senior Researcher Huxtable next attempted
to test SCP-5031’s coexistence with other

02:12:53.019 --> 02:12:58.919
living subjects, each time making sure that
the creature had been adequately fed to avoid

02:12:58.919 --> 02:13:00.920
any unseemly incidents.

02:13:00.920 --> 02:13:04.130
First, a live chicken was introduced.

02:13:04.130 --> 02:13:09.320
SCP-5031 rolled its bowling ball at high speed
towards the chicken, increasing both its and

02:13:09.320 --> 02:13:14.539
the chicken’s stress levels, and inadvertently
killing the chicken in the process.

02:13:14.539 --> 02:13:19.869
When a second chicken was introduced, SCP-5031
gently rolled a basketball towards it but

02:13:19.869 --> 02:13:24.309
ceased any further engagement after the chicken
squawked from being hit by the ball.

02:13:24.309 --> 02:13:28.739
Next to be introduced into the enclosure was
a blindfolded D Class staff member, who was

02:13:28.739 --> 02:13:33.630
instructed to sit down and roll the basketball
towards SCP-5031.

02:13:33.630 --> 02:13:38.149
After doing so for several minutes, the creature
began to approach the D class subject, who

02:13:38.149 --> 02:13:42.050
was instructed to remove their blindfold to
cease the creature’s existence and prevent

02:13:42.050 --> 02:13:44.479
any potentially deadly incidents.

02:13:44.479 --> 02:13:50.380
Finally, Researcher Huxtable had another Class-D
engage in a game of catch with SCP-5031 while

02:13:50.380 --> 02:13:53.199
facing away from the creature.

02:13:53.199 --> 02:13:58.599
This test proceeded successfully, and Senior
Researcher Huxtable remarked how SCP-5031’s

02:13:58.599 --> 02:14:00.639
motor skills were improving.

02:14:00.639 --> 02:14:06.840
Albeit gradually, and with some gentle encouragement,
through Huxtable’s tests the creature was

02:14:06.840 --> 02:14:07.840
learning.

02:14:07.840 --> 02:14:14.090
The next test, focused on teaching SCP-5031
linguistic symbols, utilized LCD displays

02:14:14.090 --> 02:14:16.949
and buttons connected to a food dispenser.

02:14:16.949 --> 02:14:21.280
One display showed an image of a rock, and
the other an image of a rotisserie chicken.

02:14:21.280 --> 02:14:26.469
After some brief probing, SCP-5031 was quickly
able to understand that pressing the button

02:14:26.469 --> 02:14:30.329
under the correct display would dispense a
rotisserie chicken for it to eat.

02:14:30.329 --> 02:14:34.960
The creature was later able to adapt when,
the following day, the screen displays and

02:14:34.960 --> 02:14:39.479
materials dispensed were swapped, and then
later set to swap at random intervals.

02:14:39.479 --> 02:14:43.920
When additional rock-dispensing stations were
introduced, this time displaying the word

02:14:43.920 --> 02:14:49.709
‘rock’ as opposed to an image, SCP-5031
was able to determine which station dispensed

02:14:49.709 --> 02:14:52.559
‘chicken’ through a process of elimination.

02:14:52.559 --> 02:14:57.369
Whenever the functions and displays were swapped,
SCP-5031 would find whichever displayed the

02:14:57.369 --> 02:14:59.659
word ‘chicken’ to receive its food.

02:14:59.659 --> 02:15:05.769
The final phase of this test presented SCP-5031
with a single station, displaying the word

02:15:05.769 --> 02:15:09.530
‘chicken’, but with a button that would
remain inactive unless the creature spelled

02:15:09.530 --> 02:15:14.409
out the same word with a collection of lettered
blocks it was provided with.

02:15:14.409 --> 02:15:18.689
After some initial confusion and frustration
as to why the button would not dispense food

02:15:18.689 --> 02:15:25.149
when pressed, SCP-5031 was able to assemble
the word correctly, not only activating the

02:15:25.149 --> 02:15:29.809
button and dispensing food, but proving to
Researcher Huxtable that the creature was

02:15:29.809 --> 02:15:32.519
capable of learning language.

02:15:32.519 --> 02:15:37.329
Huxtable continued to test the creature, encouraging
it to spell words using lettered blocks as

02:15:37.329 --> 02:15:39.050
a method of communicating.

02:15:39.050 --> 02:15:44.789
By increasing SCP-5031’s vocabulary and
the amount of human interaction it received,

02:15:44.789 --> 02:15:51.760
Senior Researcher Huxtable observed that SCP-5031
was gradually learning to sing - albeit nonverbally

02:15:51.760 --> 02:15:56.860
- as well as to juggle with its six hands
and was even communicating its own food preferences

02:15:56.860 --> 02:15:58.840
and dish pairings.

02:15:58.840 --> 02:16:06.789
Later, another Class-D, D-52125, was introduced
to SCP-5031’s enclosure to aid in further

02:16:06.789 --> 02:16:07.789
testing.

02:16:07.789 --> 02:16:12.959
Through D-52125’s instructions, the creature
quickly learned to draw using crayons, and

02:16:12.959 --> 02:16:20.249
created artworks depicting itself, its newfound
friend D-52125, Researcher Huxtable, a cat

02:16:20.249 --> 02:16:22.599
and a rotisserie chicken.

02:16:22.599 --> 02:16:27.489
SCP-5031’s new creative side didn’t stop
there though, as the creature quickly learned

02:16:27.489 --> 02:16:33.139
to play Chopsticks in only two days once a
piano was introduced into the enclosure.

02:16:33.139 --> 02:16:39.360
SCP-5031 even managed to start creating its
own original, admittedly crude, compositions.

02:16:39.360 --> 02:16:45.870
Next, a spice rack was placed inside the creature’s
cell and D-52125 demonstrated how to season

02:16:45.870 --> 02:16:46.870
meat.

02:16:46.870 --> 02:16:52.420
This proved to be SCP-5031’s new favorite
hobby, as it spent the next three days experimenting

02:16:52.420 --> 02:16:58.290
with different combinations of foods and spices,
using its letter blocks to request ‘more,

02:16:58.290 --> 02:17:00.291
more, more’ garlic powder.

02:17:00.291 --> 02:17:06.750
Interestingly, the creature only created artwork
or music when D-52125 was present, but seemed

02:17:06.750 --> 02:17:11.420
to thoroughly enjoy its experimentation with
food when left alone.

02:17:11.420 --> 02:17:17.400
Following this development, Senior Researcher
Huxtable devised a new test for SCP-5031.

02:17:17.400 --> 02:17:23.580
Providing the creature with cooking utensils
and using D-52125 to demonstrate, 5031 was

02:17:23.580 --> 02:17:28.679
shown how to prepare a variety of different
dishes, from hamburgers and tacos, to Mongolian

02:17:28.679 --> 02:17:32.389
Beef, steak, clam chowder and profiteroles.

02:17:32.389 --> 02:17:38.960
In addition to a small peanut allergy, this
eighth test revealed SCP-5031 to be a phenomenal

02:17:38.960 --> 02:17:43.350
chef, possessing culinary skills far beyond
the average person.

02:17:43.350 --> 02:17:47.790
The creature quickly and enthusiastically
embraced its newfound talents, concocting

02:17:47.790 --> 02:17:54.000
its very own brand-new recipes, with D-52125
even volunteering to be the first to taste

02:17:54.000 --> 02:17:55.930
test 5031’s dishes.

02:17:55.930 --> 02:18:03.610
It was shortly after this test that SCP-5031
spoke its very first word, and it should come

02:18:03.610 --> 02:18:07.030
as no surprise that the word was ‘salt’.

02:18:07.030 --> 02:18:11.300
Naturally, Senior Researcher Huxtable was
very proud of the progress the creature had

02:18:11.300 --> 02:18:13.380
made with its development.

02:18:13.380 --> 02:18:16.980
The final test almost seemed to be what the
creature was born for.

02:18:16.980 --> 02:18:22.650
Over the course of two months, SCP-5031 was
tasked with creating a full three-course meal

02:18:22.650 --> 02:18:26.160
which would then be served to Foundation staff
for Thanksgiving.

02:18:26.160 --> 02:18:32.421
SCP-5031 not only rose to the task, but exceeded
all of Researcher Huxtable’s expectations,

02:18:32.421 --> 02:18:37.170
creating a meal that even Gordon Ramsey would
be hard pressed to find fault with.

02:18:37.170 --> 02:18:42.750
The creature created a first course consisting
of sweet potato miso soup seasoned with turmeric.

02:18:42.750 --> 02:18:47.570
Next came a beautiful duck confit, glazed
luxuriously with apple cider and topped generously

02:18:47.570 --> 02:18:52.170
with sweet cranberry compote, paired with
a side of butternut squash gnocchi and served

02:18:52.170 --> 02:18:55.030
on a bed of kale seasoned with truffle salt.

02:18:55.030 --> 02:19:00.200
The grand finale of the exquisite meal was
a spiced cassava pie for dessert, complemented

02:19:00.200 --> 02:19:05.030
with the finest French vanilla ice cream and
a maple-hazelnut syrup.

02:19:05.030 --> 02:19:11.340
And SCP-5031 didn’t stop there, the creature
also debuted one of its original musical compositions

02:19:11.340 --> 02:19:14.380
to compliment the decadent meal it had created.

02:19:14.380 --> 02:19:20.540
As the staff enjoyed the food, SCP-5031 performed
live from its enclosure the deeply moving

02:19:20.540 --> 02:19:27.001
Piano Concerto for Six Hands, to an overwhelmingly
positive response from not only Senior Researcher

02:19:27.001 --> 02:19:30.440
Huxtable, but the entire Foundation staff.

02:19:30.440 --> 02:19:34.780
As a fitting end to the creature’s tale,
Huxtable reported that, during the Thanksgiving

02:19:34.780 --> 02:19:41.180
banquet it had created, SCP-5031’s stress
levels reduced entirely.

02:19:41.180 --> 02:19:46.280
New kinder containment measures that would
keep 5031 safer but also far more contented

02:19:46.280 --> 02:19:48.540
were submitted for approval.

02:19:48.540 --> 02:19:53.010
Perhaps some of you may find it refreshing
to learn that SCP-5031 isn’t simply just

02:19:53.010 --> 02:19:57.181
another malicious, malevolent monster that
the Foundation has to keep under lock and

02:19:57.181 --> 02:19:59.841
key for the safety of the world.

02:19:59.841 --> 02:20:05.920
Instead, SCP-5031 is a gentle – if a little
frightening at first creature - that just

02:20:05.920 --> 02:20:12.110
requires careful and considered guidance instead
of a cold iron cage and around-the-clock armed

02:20:12.110 --> 02:20:13.110
guards.

02:20:13.110 --> 02:20:17.680
Through testing, Senior Researcher Stanley
Huxtable and his fellow Foundation staff were

02:20:17.680 --> 02:20:23.041
not only able to help the creature develop,
but also found what makes it tick; and not

02:20:23.041 --> 02:20:25.591
just for the purposes of containing it.

02:20:25.591 --> 02:20:32.070
Instead, it is hoped that SCP-5031’s creativity
and flair for culinary and musical masterpieces

02:20:32.070 --> 02:20:37.840
can continue to thrive and grow, under the
proud watch of Researcher Huxtable.

02:20:37.840 --> 02:20:43.070
Now for something from the more terrifying
archives of the SCP Foundation Check out “SCP

02:20:43.070 --> 02:20:47.880
– 096 - The Shy Guy” or “SCP-106 - The
Old Man”

